{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers","id":1185538,"title":"Kickstarter Preview Discussion: \u00c6on 01-06 [Spoilers]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-13T04:39:03-08:00","id":1185538,"title":"Kickstarter Preview Discussion: \u00c6on 01-06 [Spoilers]","content":"The first public Update contains a link to &quot;Unity,&quot; the introductory fiction to the <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b> rulebook.<br /> <br /> The latest backer-only Update contains a link to the first section of the <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b> rulebook, including the Introduction, Chapter 1: History &amp; Background, Chapter 2: Earth &amp; Luna. Feel free to discuss below.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T06:18:23-08:00","id":1185559,"title":"","content":"EDIT : My mistake, sorry people. Great job on the Commonwealth write-up and I'm looking forward to the rules for Quantakinetics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 02-13-2018, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T06:21:19-08:00","id":1185561,"title":"","content":"*Problem solved. Need to read faster.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","user":"NullApostle","date":". 02-13-2018, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T06:44:51-08:00","id":1185562,"title":"","content":"I can find no instances of &quot;Bharti&quot; but 19 instances of &quot;Bharati.&quot; I'm not sure where you're seeing that.<br /> <br /> &quot;Bharati Commonwealth&quot; dates back to the original release of Aeon in 1997.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T07:03:15-08:00","id":1185567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1185562#post1185562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can find no instances of &quot;Bharti&quot; but 19 instances of &quot;Bharati.&quot; I'm not sure where you're seeing that.<br /> <br /> &quot;Bharati Commonwealth&quot; dates back to the original release of Aeon in 1997.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am so sorry... I'm have no idea why my brain went through that entire passage reading it as Bharti <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. My mistake... great job on it though, I enjoyed reading it thoroughly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T07:04:28-08:00","id":1185568,"title":"","content":"Wanted to make sure: Pakistan's an oppressive regime (as mentioned in the Middle East section) which's part of the Bharati Commonwealth, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T08:47:10-08:00","id":1186322,"title":"","content":"First I want to say that I would very much like you to know how annoyed I am that your Trinity Continuum is a much cooler name than I'd given to the WW/OP Omniverse I've slowly been unveiling to my players over the last year and a half.<br /> <br /> Secondly, will the Aeon chapter featuring how to build Aberrants as antagonists offer enough guidance that once could conceivably convert 1E Aberrant powers to start playing an Aberrant style game sooner rather than later; or will it be more like the version of Aberrants as represented in 1E Trinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T09:42:55-08:00","id":1186337,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23889\" data-vbnamecard=\"23889\">dirtypoolfilms</a> it's been mentioned that the Aberrants in Aeon are the 1st Ed variety (sub-mutant space-mad types). The dedicated future Aberrant RPG will contain Nova era powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T09:47:39-08:00","id":1186338,"title":"","content":"I presumed as much, I was just ever hopeful that at least an approximation of Nova play might be available","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T04:18:56-08:00","id":1186608,"title":"","content":"The latest backer-only Update contains a link to the second section of the <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b> rulebook, including the Introduction, Chapter 3: Space, and Chapter 4: Character Creation. Feel free to discuss below.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T10:11:44-08:00","id":1186710,"title":"","content":"Some random thoughts:<br /> <br /> Chapter 3<br /> page 14: While it is common for super heroes to use names that describe their powers, it feels weird to have the novas use names which describe their function in Eden's society. It feels as if serving Eden's society is their prime function. Perhaps a Mega-Charismatic (or their 2nd Edition equivalent) nova has used his powers to shape his fellow novas and the baselines into this weird but functioning society.<br /> <br /> page 21: Yes, thank you, the fight between the novas and the Chromatics sounds now much more realistic.<br /> <br /> Chapter 4<br /> page 1: Step 5 is printed twice<br /> <br /> - Is there a limit to the number of Auxiliary Modes you can have?<br /> - Can you later buy more Auxiliary Modes?<br /> - Do you need Psi 3 for Teleportation and Quantakinesis Auxiliary Modes?<br /> <br /> - Tier 3 Proxy Level Psions: Thank you for including them. I dislike it when NPCs like the Proxies can have powers that PCs can't get.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4081-thomas-weinbrenner","name":"Thomas Weinbrenner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T12:48:51-08:00","id":1186785,"title":"","content":"I posted this on the kickstarter comments, but I'll also ask it here worded differently. <br /> <br /> If you have three dots or more in a skill at character creation, do you get a free skill trick? Because TCore seemed to say NO, but the wording in \u00c6on chapter three seems to say YES.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T13:02:47-08:00","id":1186790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186710#post1186710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Is there a limit to the number of Auxiliary Modes you can have?<br /> - Can you later buy more Auxiliary Modes?<br /> - Do you need Psi 3 for Teleportation and Quantakinesis Auxiliary Modes?</div> </div> </div> </div>- No, but you can only have one dot per Mode. (Or to put it another way - Yes, 21 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> - Yes.<br /> - Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T13:08:57-08:00","id":1186791,"title":"","content":"I have already commented on kickstarter but I\u2019d like to contact the authors for this: Ruan\u2019s world to have it\u2019s sun seemly unmoving should be tidally locked instead of not spinning otherwise it\u2019s day length is equivalent to the year length. I think its important to have it corrected in the final version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T14:31:44-08:00","id":1186821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186710#post1186710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Tier 3 Proxy Level Psions: Thank you for including them. I dislike it when NPCs like the Proxies can have powers that PCs can't get.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It will be interesting to see how Players can reach this Tier of Power. The Proxies who are already at this level have a unique reason for it (I'm currently assuming this is a 2nd Ed mechanic based on the influence they were receiving in 1st Ed), so justifying it for Players will be interesting since it is highly unlikely that the Players used the same method (as doing so would likely make the players privy to spoiler information of the setting... like who is actually backing the Proxies). My guess would be that the players would be some of the few naturally gifted Psiads who came by their powers naturally rather than have them enhanced by the Prometheus Chambers as Psions are (or at least something to this effect).<br /> <br /> Whether any of this information is revealed in the Aeon book or future releases... only time will tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T14:41:21-08:00","id":1186824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186821#post1186821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It will be interesting to see how Players can reach this Tier of Power.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character creation backer preview explicitly tells you how. Spend experience. Reach Psi 6, meet the minimum number of dots in Modes, and there you are.<br /> <br /> While as you say, the current Proxies may be assumed to have taken a slightly different path, there's no (out of character) mystery to how anyone else gets there in 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186821#post1186821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess would be that the players would be some of the few naturally gifted Psiads who came by their powers naturally rather than have them enhanced by the Prometheus Chambers as Psions are (or at least something to this effect).<br /> <br /> Whether any of this information is revealed in the Aeon book or future releases... only time will tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>From your guess above, am I correct in assuming you haven't read the backer previews? Or did you miss the part that details the process? (Easy enough to do.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T14:43:53-08:00","id":1186825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186791#post1186791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have already commented on kickstarter but I\u2019d like to contact the authors for this: Ruan\u2019s world to have it\u2019s sun seemly unmoving should be tidally locked instead of not spinning otherwise it\u2019s day length is equivalent to the year length. I think its important to have it corrected in the final version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the catch, Starkiller. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T15:40:11-08:00","id":1186849,"title":"","content":"Everyone seem to be thinking that having the Quantakinetics in the core book was the &quot;Big Spoiler&quot; but I don't think that is it. The fact that all 8 types of Aptitude would be in the core was semi spoiled long before we were teased about something big in today's preview. One thing that no one else seems to have noticed, or commented on, is that it appears that we will be getting proxy tier powers in this book. Otherwise why bother to have the XP costs for them, or the rules for Tier 3 (Proxy) characters...<br /> <br /> *Never mind... I just went to the KS comments and apparently QK's available as PC's was the big thing. I think it's nice, and cool, but I wouldn't personally call it a &quot;big&quot; thing. Then again, Trinity was my least favorite of the 3 settings by far, so I payed it the least attention back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 02-16-2018, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T15:43:25-08:00","id":1186851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186849#post1186849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone seem to be thinking that having the Quantakinetics in the core book was the &quot;Big Spoiler&quot; but I don't think that is it. The fact that all 8 types of Aptitude would be in the core was semi spoiled long before we were teased about something big in today's preview. One thing that no one else seems to have noticed, or commented on, is that it appears that we will be getting proxy tier powers in this book. Otherwise why bother to have the XP costs for them, or the rules for Tier 3 (Proxy) characters...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean, we knew that was likely. Ian (or John?) has said that Proxy power would be attainable before today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T15:47:23-08:00","id":1186853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186851#post1186851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I mean, we knew that was likely. Ian (or John?) has said that Proxy power would be attainable before today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attainable yes, but there was no reason to think that it would be in the core rules. In a supplement, sure, but not in the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T17:32:37-08:00","id":1186878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186849#post1186849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone seem to be thinking that having the Quantakinetics in the core book was the &amp;quot;Big Spoiler&amp;quot; but I don't think that is it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was what John intended, but people may also notice that the names of all the Modes have also been disclosed. (Though there\u2019s a typo in Psycholocation, oops.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T18:16:21-08:00","id":1186890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186878#post1186878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was what John intended, but people may also notice that the names of all the Modes have also been disclosed. (Though there\u2019s a typo in Psycholocation, oops.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but do the modes do similar things to their 1st edition counterparts, and are the QK's similar to their fan made supplement?<br /> <br /> *I'm not looking for exact details, that will come in time, I'm looking for generalities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T18:47:51-08:00","id":1186897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186890#post1186890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but do the modes do similar things to their 1st edition counterparts,</div> </div> </div> </div>The ones that are the same name, mostly yes. The ones with different names, some yes, some no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186890#post1186890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and are the QK's similar to their fan made supplement?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea. I\u2019ve never read a fan supplement with them in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186890#post1186890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*I'm not looking for exact details, that will come in time, I'm looking for generalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general sense of similarities, my first step in building the new system was to work out the basic dice resolution mechanic. My second step was to sit down with every published power for the Aptitudes, see what worked, what didn\u2019t, what was less thematic, more thematic, which were speed bumps, which worked well within Storypath, which didn\u2019t work at all in Storypath, what to do about those that didn\u2019t work in Storypath.<br /> <br /> From that, I put a lot of effort into distilling the core essence of each Mode and the powers that should be within each one, and calibrated what level of power each dot should provide. (Importantly, keeping in mind the new resolution system.) <br /> <br /> From there, I figured out where the gaps were and what powers should fill those gaps. This required tweaking quite a few Modes, and writing some from scratch.<br /> <br /> A couple of Modes are distillations of more than one previous Mode. Thermokinesis is one example - 1E Cryokinesis was rather poor, and there was no real reason why it and Pyrokinesis needed to be separate. (IMO)<br /> <br /> Overall, just about everything Aptitudes could do in 1E they can do in 2E. (A few exceptions exist, and we can talk more about them soon, because I expect the next backer preview will have the rules chapters.) Every Aptitude can do more than what 1E had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186890#post1186890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but do the modes do similar things to their 1st edition counterparts,</div> </div> </div> </div>tl;dr - Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T19:15:47-08:00","id":1186903,"title":"","content":"So what tier are Psions supposed to be by default? Aeon preview 2 says that both Talents and Psions are Tier 2. But, the Core preview says that Talents are Tier 2 and Psions are Tier 3. Which is correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T19:41:43-08:00","id":1186910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186903#post1186903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what tier are Psions supposed to be by default? Aeon preview 2 says that both Talents and Psions are Tier 2. But, the Core preview says that Talents are Tier 2 and Psions are Tier 3. Which is correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Psions and Talents are Tier 2. Proxies and Novas are Tier 3, Aberrants are Tier 4.<br /> <br /> I think this may be a case of the core preview listing Mundane-Talent-Psion-Proxy-Nova-Aberrant as individual rows on the table (on page 3), rather than grouping them by Tier, or having a column that spelled out what Tier they were. <br /> <br /> If I\u2019ve missed another section of the Core preview that lists it otherwise, please point me in It\u2019s direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T20:24:04-08:00","id":1186915,"title":"","content":"Looks like that may be the problem. I was looking at the table on page 3 of Core preview 2. Thanks for clearing that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T20:29:35-08:00","id":1186917,"title":"","content":"Are Talents understood to exist in Universe by the people in Universe or do they come off as &quot;mundane&quot; outside Nihon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T20:32:52-08:00","id":1186918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186910#post1186910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psions and Talents are Tier 2. Proxies and Novas are Tier 3, Aberrants are Tier 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that they aren't written yet, but would you put Stalwarts (Adventure!'s Novas) at Tier 2?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T21:19:44-08:00","id":1186932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186917#post1186917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Talents understood to exist in Universe by the people in Universe</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I think John or Ian has mentioned something about Clarisentients sometimes getting a \u2018vibe\u2019 around strong Talents, but nothing definable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186917#post1186917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> or do they come off as &amp;quot;mundane&amp;quot; outside Nihon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mundane. I don\u2019t understand the part about Nihon, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T21:21:09-08:00","id":1186934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186918#post1186918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that they aren't written yet, but would you put Stalwarts (Adventure!'s Novas) at Tier 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really have no idea. But since Talents are Tier 2, and Stalwarts, Mesmerists and Talents were all roughly equal in 1E Adventure!, it seems like a reasonable guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T21:34:07-08:00","id":1186935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186932#post1186932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. I think John or Ian has mentioned something about Clarisentients sometimes getting a \u2018vibe\u2019 around strong Talents, but nothing definable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mundane. I don\u2019t understand the part about Nihon, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e Nihon unlocked some of the secrets of the Aberrant/psion/Talent Genome. They could safely erupt you and were secretly hiding a bunch of megaints on the islands. They also found out you could flip the switch another way so a person wouldn't become a psion or Nova and become a &quot;Superior&quot; which were Daredevils/Talents in 1e. <br /> <br /> Superiors are Brought up on the preview so I was wondering if basically Nihon being the only group that knows about Paramorphs(outside Max and Aeon who think he's the only one becuase he's the only tier 3?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T22:17:46-08:00","id":1186941,"title":"","content":"Okay, I understand what you\u2019re asking now, thanks. <br /> <br /> Briefly, and working from 1E principles, Nihon working out how to make Superiors doesn\u2019t necessarily mean they know or understand anything else about Talents, how they work, or how to detect the ones they haven\u2019t specifically made into Superiors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T23:44:46-08:00","id":1186959,"title":"","content":"No one in the \u00c6on era really understands any more about Talents than they do in the modern era -- and given the presence of psions, most people are more concerned with figuring the ins and outs of how psi and the subquantum universe work.<br /> <br /> Powerful clairsentients can sometimes detect an extra &quot;oomph&quot; around Talents, due to their bending the strings of Fate (or perhaps Fate bends the Talent). But even then it's not enough to definitively say anything is particularly different about them. The \u00c6on Trinity, however, remains one of the most popular employers of Talents, whether by design or by happenstance. They probably know most about the phenomenon, if it is one, but even then they don't know much. It's entirely likely that Max remains the sole identifiable paramorph.<br /> <br /> Nihonjin Superiors are a weird case: they may be the 22nd century equivalent of stalwarts -- novas erupted and locked at a low (&quot;safe&quot;) level of power. Or they may be a particular flavour of paramorph that doesn't usually fall under the header of &quot;Talent.&quot; Either way, Nakamura-san and his contemporaries are barely scratching the surface: they don't know about Talents beyond the bounds of their own research, and don't have a handle on the larger implications of their work beyond finding a safe alternative to eruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T00:06:14-08:00","id":1186968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186959#post1186959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nihonjin Superiors are a weird case: they may be the 22nd century equivalent of stalwarts -- novas erupted and locked at a low (&quot;safe&quot;) level of power. Or they may be a particular flavour of paramorph that doesn't usually fall under the header of &quot;Talent.&quot; Either way, Nakamura-san and his contemporaries are barely scratching the surface: they don't know about Talents beyond the bounds of their own research, and don't have a handle on the larger implications of their work beyond finding a safe alternative to eruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>So more focus might come on them later but for now Talent Nihon agents will cover that ground?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T07:26:10-08:00","id":1187036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186824#post1186824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From your guess above, am I correct in assuming you haven't read the backer previews? Or did you miss the part that details the process? (Easy enough to do.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've read through the mechanics of character creation... and much of the setting material... and while it explains how to create a Tier 3 character, it doesn't give an in-game reasoning for such Proxy- level Player characters to exist.<br /> <br /> When i build a character, i like to understand the setting reasoning for them being better than the average person of their type. We have in setting reasons for the Proxies to be Tier 3... and know why nearly every other Psion in the setting is only Tier 2... but i have yet to see any in-game reasoning for a PC to be Tier 3 (same level as the Proxies) without undergoing the same process they did (which, at least in 1st Ed, was not quite the same as other Psions).<br /> <br /> If you've run across an in-setting explanation that they have already provided (not game mechanics but and actual reason why some Psions would have Proxy-level powers), then please, share that information with us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T08:03:34-08:00","id":1187044,"title":"","content":"I think you're being held back a bit by 1e thinking, Shadowstripe.<br /> <br /> In 1e, proxies and psions were technically different things: the processes used to create them were different. Psions were latents that basically got a genetic spit-shine to let them do their thing better, while Proxies got mixed with bits of Doyen DNA in order to do things better than any human was <i>capable</i>, Prometheus Chamber or not. Technically speaking, they were hybrids, although they probably wouldn't want to quantify it like that.<br /> <br /> That's no longer the case.<br /> <br /> In the new edition, proxies and psions are fundamentally the same thing. Any psion, through enough dedication to their noetic abilities, can rise to proxy-level. The proxies themselves just got to skip that middle bit and got awakened to their full potential all at once. There's no in-setting justification needed for &quot;people getting better at what they do.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the years since the Sydney attack, there are few, if any, other psions who have risen to their level. Maybe someone like Ellayne Cassel, or a couple of other &quot;number twos&quot; who have been with their orders for a long time.<br /> <br /> But the capability is there, if PCs want to claim it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T08:19:31-08:00","id":1187047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1187044#post1187044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the capability is there, if PCs want to claim it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to underline this last bit's importance. This is not a mid-'90s product (he said, with some guilty culpability) in which the NPCs are faster, stronger, smarter, prettier, wittier, and cooler than the PCs will ever be.<br /> <br /> - C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T08:49:25-08:00","id":1187049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1187036#post1187036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've run across an in-setting explanation that they have already provided (not game mechanics but and actual reason why some Psions would have Proxy-level powers), then please, share that information with us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I come at al this a little differently. For what its worth (as someone quite passionate about 1st Ed and 90s games generally), I like that the rules are there in 2nd ed to allow PCs, over time, to become as powerful as Proxies if they want to. <br /> <br /> But there's a <i>whole lot more</i> to being and remaining an actual Proxy than something facilitated in powers and scale rules to my mind. Should PC's want to become the setting equivalent they of Proxies the stories told by the group become the in-game reason, with one important caveat: <i>should they actually succeed</i>. <br /> <br /> As both a player and GM I don't subscribe to the idea that PC's must always, eventually, &quot;win/succeed/can do whatever they want&quot;. But I do subscribe to the idea that while PC's should not be held back in rules terms from trying to reach their goals, there will be real-world consequences to the <i>actions</i> they take trying to get there and they may be their own undoing. The 2nd edition take on current Proxies seems to suggest they <i>remain</i> Proxies because of their personalities, considerable skills, exceptional judgment &amp; decision making skills, allies, resources, and yes their powers too. They are replaceable, but it will take remarkable people without taking into account their powers.<br /> <br /> I can think of, maybe, 2 characters in a dozen or so campaigns of Aeon whose personalities maybe would lend themselves to being Proxies for longer than a day if they attained the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T13:55:57-08:00","id":1187133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1187044#post1187044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're being held back a bit by 1e thinking, Shadowstripe.<br /> <br /> In 1e, proxies and psions were technically different things: the processes used to create them were different. Psions were latents that basically got a genetic spit-shine to let them do their thing better, while Proxies got mixed with bits of Doyen DNA in order to do things better than any human was <i>capable</i>, Prometheus Chamber or not. Technically speaking, they were hybrids, although they probably wouldn't want to quantify it like that.<br /> <br /> That's no longer the case.<br /> <br /> In the new edition, proxies and psions are fundamentally the same thing. Any psion, through enough dedication to their noetic abilities, can rise to proxy-level. The proxies themselves just got to skip that middle bit and got awakened to their full potential all at once. There's no in-setting justification needed for &quot;people getting better at what they do.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the years since the Sydney attack, there are few, if any, other psions who have risen to their level. Maybe someone like Ellayne Cassel, or a couple of other &quot;number twos&quot; who have been with their orders for a long time.<br /> <br /> But the capability is there, if PCs want to claim it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I was thinking that there would be some hold over from 1st Ed as to why the Proxies are more powerful than regular Psions and that if players can reach that level, there would also be a similar reason (not the same reason of course).<br /> <br /> So while Psions start off as Tier 2 they can all eventually reach Tier 3 with experience (from my calculations of the needed requirements, about 120 experience). I wonder if Talents will also be able to increase their Tier to 3 (can't see anything to support or prevent such from what I've read, so it could go either way I would say depending on what is needed).<br /> <br /> This does help in building characters, it means that while it has yet to happen with most of the regular Psions, it is likely only a matter of time before others cross the threshold to Proxie-level Tier 3 status.<br /> <br /> Still... it does make one wonder about Psiads... those who manage to unlock their psychic potential without the need of a Prometheus Chamber... will the possibility for such characters be present in the Aeon setting in a future product... or with it get its own era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T14:44:54-08:00","id":1187141,"title":"","content":"Assuming the lore about him is loosely the same, I wonder if Maxwell is a tier 3 Paramorph/Talent...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T17:09:11-08:00","id":1187171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1187141#post1187141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the lore about him is loosely the same, I wonder if Maxwell is a tier 3 Paramorph/Talent...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a very good question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T18:21:41-08:00","id":1187187,"title":"","content":"Psions and Psiads are considered the same Tier, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T18:32:49-08:00","id":1187193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1187133#post1187133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I was thinking that there would be some hold over from 1st Ed as to why the Proxies are more powerful than regular Psions and that if players can reach that level, there would also be a similar reason (not the same reason of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Setting Secrets chapter goes into some more detail about it, but I won\u2019t say anything more about that here... yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T02:45:54-08:00","id":1187253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1187193#post1187193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Setting Secrets chapter goes into some more detail about it, but I won\u2019t say anything more about that here... yet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest, i was expecting as much (that many of the behind the scenes details would be in that chapter and that it wouldn't be discussed until it was released). I tend to assume that things between Editions of a game will generally be similar until the newest edition says otherwise (or someone in the know of the latest lore/information reveals such).<br /> <br /> In 1st Ed, Proxies were more than mere human thanks to the Doyen... thus could achieve higher levels of power than human Psions. Now it appears in 2nd Ed, that the Proxies merely became advanced Psions (again, likely because of the Doyen if they are still working behind the scenes) and that all Human Psions have the potential to reach this same level of power (though without the Doyen advancing their abilities like with the Proxies, it will take longer to unlock this potential).<br /> <br /> I am hoping that we will get rules for the rare Psiads who unlock their potential on their own.<br /> <br /> For now, I think i have a few ideas I can work with for creating them until official rules are provided. First, since Psiads do not use Prometheus Chambers to unlock their potential, they are not limited to a single Psi Aptitude... meaning they can learn any and all the various psi abilities given time. However, this also means they don't favor any particular Aptitude either and treat all modes within a given Aptitude as Auxiliary Modes when it comes to purchasing them (thus requiring more experience to master any one Aptitude compared to a Psion, but can master more than one). Additionally, since they don't use the Prometheus Chambers, they don't get the bonuses the Chambers provide Psions (the bonus Attribute dot or raising their initial Psi rating to 3 from 2). This means that all Psiads will start a little weaker than Psions (they start at Psi 2 and have one less attribute dot compared to Psions), but can become significantly more powerful over time with their ability to master multiple Aptitudes if they so choose. Since they start at Psi 2, they can not learn Quantakinesis or Teleportation modes to begin with (but can pick them up once they raise their Psi to 3). Of course, like any Psion, they run the risk of psionic dysfunction if a mode in any Aptitude they know is 3 dots higher than the next highest mode in that Aptitude (which can be a problem if they are learning multiple Aptitudes at once... though each Aptitude is treated separately).<br /> <br /> I wonder how close these rough ideas will be to the official rules when they are provided (in the Setting Secrets chapter perhaps... or a future product maybe?)... if we ever get them that is. For now these are just speculations and may or may not be present in my games (provided no official rules for Psiads are provided). I wonder if anyone has any ideas on how the established Psi-Orders would react to a Psiad being discovered who has developed their powers independently from their teachings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I love speculating in these areas... as they lead to all sorts of interesting questions and such, but perhaps it is best left for its own thread.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, looking forward to the next backer manuscript reveal and to see what other stretch goals will be unlocked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T02:51:54-08:00","id":1187255,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s remember to pick up this conversation again when the appropriate previews are released. I\u2019d love to continue the discussion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Regarding Psiads - They\u2019ve been mentioned as a stretch goal, but not added to the list with a dollar figure yet. When they are, if we get them unlocked, we\u2019ll see the rules relatively soonish as they\u2019ll appear in the expansion. If not, then it will take longer as they\u2019ll have to fit into some other supplement later.<br /> <br /> Personally, I hope we get to whatever the goal is and get them sooner rather than later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T06:56:21-08:00","id":1187277,"title":"","content":"So, minor mechanical note - The Psion template re-introduces the old issue where the order in which you buy things matters. It's only a trivial amount, but literally every character should be taking an extra dot in Psi from the Prometheus Chamber and then if you really need it, buying that Attribute later to save 2 experience. Not a big deal, but a bit weird that there's a hard-and-fast mechanically optimum route.<br /> <br /> Also, I like that most characters should be starting with 20 experience. That's a lot of options (And if you followed the advice above means that you can start at Psi 4, with an extra Mode dot, if you're going full bore on the Psi abilities. Or you can start with Psi 3 and a Mode at 5, giving you Psionic Dysfunction, which was very fun in 1st ed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T08:01:21-08:00","id":1187285,"title":"","content":"In all honesty I'll probably use a little bit more Experience points to start to better reflect the experiences needed to be part of the group I use, does this mean every character will need or use this I don't know and won't until I sit down and work everything out I need to run my Exploration chronicles.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn characters being able to equal Proxies I think it is a good thing. Since in my campaign the Proxies are extremely removed this lets the PC aspire to greater heights in the stories we are telling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T05:21:12-08:00","id":1187811,"title":"","content":"The latest backer-only Update contains a link to the third section of the <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b> rulebook, including Chapter 5: Organizations, and Chapter 6: New Rules. Feel free to discuss below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T07:29:34-08:00","id":1187831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1186710#post1186710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter 3<br /> page 14: While it is common for super heroes to use names that describe their powers, it feels weird to have the novas use names which describe their function in Eden's society. It feels as if serving Eden's society is their prime function. Perhaps a Mega-Charismatic (or their 2nd Edition equivalent) nova has used his powers to shape his fellow novas and the baselines into this weird but functioning society.</div> </div> </div> </div>The younger novas on Eden actually ARE raised with the expectation that serving Eden's society is their prime, or even only function! The oldest novas there have more traditionally superheroic names. My first (way too long) draft mentioned Broadside, Adamant, and Centrifuga.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> page 21: Yes, thank you, the fight between the novas and the Chromatics sounds now much more realistic. </div> </div> </div>Thank you, revising that incident a bit was a goal!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T10:05:30-08:00","id":1187883,"title":"","content":"This is a REALLY fun one to read. the changes to the orders are really interesting, how they've been updated. ISRAs recruiting tactics, for example, make a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4941-cielago","name":"Cielago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4941_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T12:51:23-08:00","id":1187943,"title":"","content":"Still not a fan of the Legion Edge being mandatory. Ah well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T15:09:19-08:00","id":1187990,"title":"","content":"I am a little confused how one becomes a psion in relation to the Orders. As a latent do you sign up for the Order and then before being dunked have the option of swapping to a different tank or do you generally sign up with an order and some people leave and join others? Similar sort of question for freelance psychics..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T17:13:18-08:00","id":1188027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1187990#post1187990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a little confused how one becomes a psion in relation to the Orders. As a latent do you sign up for the Order and then before being dunked have the option of swapping to a different tank or do you generally sign up with an order and some people leave and join others? Similar sort of question for freelance psychics..</div> </div> </div> </div>Very quick answer (typing on phone, excuse any typos)<br /> <br /> There are hundreds of places you can be tested for latency. The Orders have testing facilities in various places (with a few exceptions like Nippon) and AEon runs more all over the place. <br /> <br /> What happens next depends on the facility and the test outcome. Most latents test with General aptitude - they'd be good at most Aptitudes. Some test strongly for one in particular. Regardless of this, anyone can be triggered into one of the basic Aptitudes (not teleportation or QK). <br /> <br /> The facility may give you a choice - be triggered into what you test strongly for, what your preference is, or whatever the Order offers. Others might encourage you to just go for their specialty regardless. <br /> <br /> Happy to expand on this in a few hours when I'm closer to q real keyboard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T23:18:44-08:00","id":1188083,"title":"","content":"So its not assumed the would be psion has some sort of debt to a group for going through the process?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T23:31:29-08:00","id":1188085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1187990#post1187990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a little confused how one becomes a psion in relation to the Orders. As a latent do you sign up for the Order and then before being dunked have the option of swapping to a different tank or do you generally sign up with an order and some people leave and join others? Similar sort of question for freelance psychics..</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, take 2 - bigger screen, bigger keyboard.<br /> <br /> The answer is that there are several pathways. You can sign up with an Order, get swapped around, or leave. None of them have a hold on you forever. I should also point out that all of this is regarding in-character perspective. Out of character, there\u2019s nothing to prevent the player making any Aptitude* Psion work for any Order (or AEon).<br /> <br /> * Barring Quantakinetics, which have a few more considerations.<br /> <br /> Building on what I said in my previous post. Say you live in a major city with a choice of testing facilities. You head over to one, looking to be tested. They discover that you\u2019re a latent. Congratulations! You might have generally even latency, or you might be strongly disposed to one Aptitude. The testing facility will discuss this with you and will probably offer to send you on for more screening to see if you can join the Order. Every Order has tests and standards that you have to pass before they\u2019ll accept you. If you\u2019re a latent and they decide you don\u2019t pass, they won\u2019t activate you, even if you have strong latency for that Aptitude. Sucks for you, but from their point better to have a disgruntled latent who might cause some minor trouble, than a disgruntled psion who might cause big trouble later on. Or, you might not meet their standards, but you\u2019ll easily pass the requirements of another Order. Then they might refer you along,<br /> <br /> If you\u2019ve tested strongly for an Aptitude other than what they do, they may offer to either arrange to have you triggered and receive basic training by the other Order, as part of the reciprocation arrangements, or you might decide that you\u2019re more interested in what they provide. Either way, you tend to have a choice. Circumstances might occasionally dictate otherwise, and you can build character backgrounds around that, but generally in 2nd edition any Aptitude can (and do) work for any Order.<br /> <br /> If you get tested for AEon, the process might be a little different. They don\u2019t have a Prometheus Chamber of their own, so they\u2019ll have to send you out for someone else to trigger. If you meet AEon\u2019s standards, they might recruit and train you, then send you for external psionic training. If you don\u2019t, or you\u2019re not interested, they\u2019ll put you in contact with the Order of your choice, and the previous process takes place.<br /> <br /> I think between the two posts I\u2019ve covered the same ground in a could of different ways. Hopefully that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T23:44:47-08:00","id":1188087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188083#post1188083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So its not assumed the would be psion has some sort of debt to a group for going through the process?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you\u2019re asking.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re asking if a character has a debt to someone simply for being triggered into an Aptitude - then generally yes, to varying degrees. Every Order has to invest time and effort into their psions, even if it\u2019s just the use of the Prometheus Chamber and basic training. If you pass screening, and they offer to trigger you, then you\u2019ll tend to have some kind of obligation. The Legions expect a three year term of service, Orgotek will have contractural expectations and penalty clauses if you leave early etc. ISRA tends to let you wander off if you want, because regardless of where you go and what you do, you\u2019re always part of the totality and therefore (in their minds) part of the broader Order.<br /> <br /> From your character\u2019s background point of view, these terms are usually short and can be woven into the story. (I did my tour of duty, then decided to go freelance when the time was up.) Or you can make it a source of conflict for your character. (I went AWOL before my tour was done, and though the Legions couldn\u2019t be bothered chasing me down, if I cross paths with them they\u2019ll probably take me in to either complete my time, or go to prison.)<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re asking whether the character has obligation beyond her Order (or AEon) if she\u2019s triggered by another Order as part of the reciprocal arrangmements, then no - all debts in this case are held by the Orders, not the individuals.<br /> <br /> Make sense? Have I answered the right question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T01:10:20-08:00","id":1188100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188085#post1188085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Barring Quantakinetics, which have a few more considerations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a question about this, I know the in game reasons for this, but are there out of game reasons as well? (ie. Are they more powerful then other Aptitudes? Are they troublesome/don't work well with others in group play, etc)<br /> <br /> Also, can you tell us what media you used as inspiration when designing the different things that an Aptitude can do/should feel like in use? (ie. Did you use the movie Jumper for the look, or feel, of Teleportation, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T01:52:00-08:00","id":1188109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188100#post1188100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about this, I know the in game reasons for this, but are there out of game reasons as well? (ie. Are they more powerful then other Aptitudes? Are they troublesome/don't work well with others in group play, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what the 1st Ed OOC reasons were. Since we never saw a complete write-up of QK, it\u2019s possible the answer was one or all of what you\u2019ve said. <br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, QK is balanced against the other Aptitudes. It\u2019s more powerful in its area of expertise, but the same is true for every aptitude. It\u2019s arguably slightly more powerful, to justify its 3 Psi minimum requirement.<br /> <br /> The QK powers are such that there are certainly reasons for others to fear them, but considering a powerful PK could break you into bloody chunks, or a powerful telepath could destroy your mind, any powerful, ill-intentioned psion is a threat.<br /> <br /> A few more days and you\u2019ll see what I mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188100#post1188100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, can you tell us what media you used as inspiration when designing the different things that an Aptitude can do/should feel like in use? (ie. Did you use the movie Jumper for the look, or feel, of Teleportation, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Trinity 1st edition was the primary point of inspiration. But for the feel of various powers... it\u2019s hard to say exactly. I have very clear images of how they work and appear in my head, and I can trace some of these back to media and inspirations, but not everything. Jumper works for teleportation, sure, but so does Dr Strange. (The rapid one-after-the-other tactical jumps with vehicles are probably beyond the power scope, but personal rapid jump isn\u2019t.) <br /> <br /> Vitakinesis drew on the Captain America MCU movies - especially the enhanced human aspects. Telepathy tends to be unflashy, but Babylon 5\u2019s Psi Corps has nailed it pretty well. Clairsentience draws on Leverage and Person of Interest, in a strange kind of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T02:15:14-08:00","id":1188113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188109#post1188109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea what the 1st Ed OOC reasons were. Since we never saw a complete write-up of QK, it\u2019s possible the answer was one or all of what you\u2019ve said.<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, QK is balanced against the other Aptitudes. It\u2019s more powerful in its area of expertise, but the same is true for every aptitude. It\u2019s arguably slightly more powerful, to justify its 3 Psi minimum requirement.<br /> <br /> The QK powers are such that there are certainly reasons for others to fear them, but considering a powerful PK could break you into bloody chunks, or a powerful telepath could destroy your mind, any powerful, ill-intentioned psion is a threat.<br /> <br /> A few more days and you\u2019ll see what I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to hear, and I'm looking forward to picking your brain on Friday.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188109#post1188109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trinity 1st edition was the primary point of inspiration. But for the feel of various powers... it\u2019s hard to say exactly. I have very clear images of how they work and appear in my head, and I can trace some of these back to media and inspirations, but not everything. Jumper works for teleportation, sure, but so does Dr Strange. (The rapid one-after-the-other tactical jumps with vehicles are probably beyond the power scope, but personal rapid jump isn\u2019t.)<br /> <br /> Vitakinesis drew on the Captain America MCU movies - especially the enhanced human aspects. Telepathy tends to be unflashy, but Babylon 5\u2019s Psi Corps has nailed it pretty well. Clairsentience draws on Leverage and Person of Interest, in a strange kind of way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have no idea how much that makes me happy. I love Captain America, he's by far my favorite hero, and to know that there is type of psionic aptitude that will allow me to play a similar character... It's awesome. Also, would Burn Notice work as inspiration for Clairsentience? The &quot;No Really, I planned for this.&quot; motif.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T03:08:23-08:00","id":1188117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188113#post1188113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have no idea how much that makes me happy. I love Captain America, he's by far my favorite hero, and to know that there is type of psionic aptitude that will allow me to play a similar character... It's awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>A reasonably powerful vitakinetic should be able to do just about everything Cap does, except for the magic shield throwing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188113#post1188113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, would Burn Notice work as inspiration for Clairsentience? The &amp;quot;No Really, I planned for this.&amp;quot; motif.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of visualizing? Yes. If you\u2019ve read the fiction they posted a week or so ago, you\u2019ve got a good sense of how I visualize the \u2018future planning\u2019 stuff. The mechanical execution is less like it, but designed to emulate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T04:22:50-08:00","id":1188128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188117#post1188117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of visualizing? Yes. If you\u2019ve read the fiction they posted a week or so ago, you\u2019ve got a good sense of how I visualize the \u2018future planning\u2019 stuff. The mechanical execution is less like it, but designed to emulate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, kind of like the Sherlock fight scene: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BGCMfprPJoA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BGCMfprPJoA</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T12:40:34-08:00","id":1188266,"title":"","content":"I'm actually kind of excited to see the finished product with art in. Will there be any art piece showing what the aeon trinity Cube looks like? I'm kinda interested in what like their headquarters look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T13:35:11-08:00","id":1188285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188087#post1188087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on what you\u2019re asking.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re asking if a character has a debt to someone simply for being triggered into an Aptitude - then generally yes, to varying degrees. Every Order has to invest time and effort into their psions, even if it\u2019s just the use of the Prometheus Chamber and basic training. If you pass screening, and they offer to trigger you, then you\u2019ll tend to have some kind of obligation. The Legions expect a three year term of service, Orgotek will have contractural expectations and penalty clauses if you leave early etc. ISRA tends to let you wander off if you want, because regardless of where you go and what you do, you\u2019re always part of the totality and therefore (in their minds) part of the broader Order.<br /> <br /> From your character\u2019s background point of view, these terms are usually short and can be woven into the story. (I did my tour of duty, then decided to go freelance when the time was up.) Or you can make it a source of conflict for your character. (I went AWOL before my tour was done, and though the Legions couldn\u2019t be bothered chasing me down, if I cross paths with them they\u2019ll probably take me in to either complete my time, or go to prison.)<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re asking whether the character has obligation beyond her Order (or AEon) if she\u2019s triggered by another Order as part of the reciprocal arrangmements, then no - all debts in this case are held by the Orders, not the individuals.<br /> <br /> Make sense? Have I answered the right question?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah that makes sense. So how invasive and time consuming is latent screening for the potential psion? Can it be done without the latent's knowledge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T13:44:07-08:00","id":1188288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188266#post1188266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be any art piece showing what the aeon trinity Cube looks like? I'm kinda interested in what like their headquarters look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't answer the art question (that would be cool!) but I feel like I should point out that the Cube contains waaaaay more than just the Neptune offices, and that Triton and Proteus have their own separate headquarters locations. And the Aeon Council could be anywhere!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T16:11:29-08:00","id":1188326,"title":"","content":"So, with all this diversification of the different Aptitudes and their associated Orders, why was the same treatment not made for Quantakinesis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:16:55-08:00","id":1188373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188326#post1188326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with all this diversification of the different Aptitudes and their associated Orders, why was the same treatment not made for Quantakinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure I understand the question, but you'll find out more about Chitra Bhanu and Quantakinesis in upcoming previews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:40:51-08:00","id":1188378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Topher Gerkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188373#post1188373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure I understand the question, but you'll find out more about Chitra Bhanu and Quantakinesis in upcoming previews.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For example there are Legion Teleporters, there are Aesclepian Teleporters. There don't seem to be Legion QKs or Norca QKs or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:42:07-08:00","id":1188379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188326#post1188326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with all this diversification of the different Aptitudes and their associated Orders, why was the same treatment not made for Quantakinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're asking what I think you're asking (why aren't Quantakinetics more widespread throughout the Orders), the short answer is 'story reasons.' That said, the current previews talk about the Chitra Bhanu purge a bit, that's a good place to start answering that question. (Upcoming previews should shed more light on the issue of Quantakinetics, but I don't know how much I can/should say at this time since that's not my call)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T20:29:51-08:00","id":1188392,"title":"","content":"While the general scope of the setting is the same, there was a major shift in the orders makeup, both in making sure that the Aptitudes and their respective orders are no longer synonyms, as well as redefining what the orders are/are like. You no longer need any justification for playing any aptitude in any order, unless you want to play a QK, then you are still hosed. With this change in editions it would have been the perfect time to introduce a handful of QK options that aren't CB or Freelance Psions.<br /> <br /> tl:dr - What Lian Said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 02-22-2018, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T00:10:17-08:00","id":1188422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188266#post1188266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually kind of excited to see the finished product with art in. Will there be any art piece showing what the aeon trinity Cube looks like? I'm kinda interested in what like their headquarters look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s on the Kickstarter campaign\u2019s front page, between the images of the core rule book and the AEon rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T00:16:37-08:00","id":1188424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188326#post1188326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with all this diversification of the different Aptitudes and their associated Orders, why was the same treatment not made for Quantakinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the other Orders hunted down the QKs and destroyed their Prometheus Chamber. Officially, they no longer exist, because they all turn into Aberrant sympathizers and traitors (according to the propaganda).<br /> <br /> Kind of hard to have QKs running around belonging to other Orders when those other Orders hunted and killed them all.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: Also, as you\u2019ll see, QKs are useful to have around. The Orders should feel kind of shit for not having them any more, which is also kind of hard to do if they do have them.<br /> <br /> There are ways to play QKs, which you\u2019ll see soon. And entire campaigns could be set around bringing them back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 02-22-2018, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T00:37:17-08:00","id":1188428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188285#post1188285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that makes sense. So how invasive and time consuming is latent screening for the potential psion? Can it be done without the latent's knowledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Lian, you ask awesome questions that I get to answer in multiple ways! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Let\u2019s break it down a little.<br /> <br /> How invasive iand time consuming is latency testing? I don\u2019t think it\u2019s every been entirely detailed, but I imagine it includes both a blood test and various cognitive tests. I\u2019d say the blood test portion only requires a very small amount of blood and looks for specific genetic markers that indicate latency and compatibility with Prometheus Chambers. I believe the cognitive tests take an hour or so and generate a profile that points out any predispositions towards certain Aptitudes. Put them both together and you get the kinds of latency tests AEon and the Orders administer.<br /> <br /> Can latency testing be done without the individual\u2019s knowledge? Sure, just look at Nippon. They test, find, and destroy without the people being any the wiser. In my mind, they only do the blood test portion (disguised as other general medical checkups) and don\u2019t care less if you have predisposition to an Aptitiude. If they find latency markers, they counter it.<br /> <br /> I think part of what you\u2019re asking is whether people can wander around with portable scanning devices to randomly test members of the public for latency. In this case, in my mind I\u2019d say no. *But*, Clairsentients can pick up on strong latency without anyone being aware of what they\u2019re doing. But there aren\u2019t that many clears, and they have better things to be doing than scanning for strong patents all the time.<br /> <br /> Summary: Testing for latency is difficult (but not impossible) to do without the person noticing. Strong latents can be detected silently, if you have a clear who could be bothered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T00:40:08-08:00","id":1188430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188424#post1188424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the other Orders hunted down the QKs and destroyed their Prometheus Chamber. Officially, they no longer exist, because they all turn into Aberrant sympathizers and traitors (according to the propaganda).<br /> <br /> Kind of hard to have QKs running around belonging to other Orders when those other Orders hunted and killed them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of my point. So much has changed with this new edition, why not change it so that there are/were QK's in other orders. Everything else can remain the same, CB going &quot;bad&quot;, getting destroyed, etc. All you have to do is throw in a line like &quot;only a handful were ever created for each of the other orders before the CB Prometheus Chamber was destroyed&quot; and &quot;these Psions are closely watched for signs of corruption by their orders.&quot; Same basic story, but now there is an option for playing a Orgotec (or any order really) game and having one of the player playing a QK. As is, your stuck playing a Freelance Psion and hoping that no other character has the Intellect above 1 that it would require to figure out that you have QK.<br /> <br /> *I just read you Edit, and your answer is a good one. I guess I will have to wait and see for the Setting Secrets chapter to see if some of my character ideas would work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 02-22-2018, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T00:51:12-08:00","id":1188432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188430#post1188430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of my point. So much has changed with this new edition, why not change it so that there are/were QK's in other orders. Everything else can remain the same, CB going &amp;quot;bad&amp;quot;, getting destroyed, etc. All you have to do is throw in a line like &amp;quot;only a handful were ever created for each of the other orders before the CB Prometheus Chamber was destroyed&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;these Psions are closely watched for signs of corruption by their orders.&amp;quot; Same basic story, but now there is an option for playing a Orgotec (or any order really) game and having one of the player playing a QK. As is, your stuck playing a Freelance Psion and hoping that no other character has the Intellect above 1 that it would require to figure out that you have QK.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were QKs in other Orders. The Orders killed them too. The reasons for this are very similar to the reasons in 1st edition, and no QK was going to be allowed to survive.<br /> <br /> And I disagree with your assertion that you\u2019re stuck with only one path for playing a QK. I know it\u2019s unfair that I have the benefit of having read what\u2019s coming, and can\u2019t just tell you all because of NDA ninjas, but soon you\u2019ll see why I disagree and we can discuss and explore the different ways together. <br /> <br /> But until you\u2019ve seen the QK powers, please don\u2019t assume that it\u2019s easy to tell that a quantakinetic isn\u2019t another psion, any more than you can spot the difference between a biokinetic and a vitakinetic if all they\u2019ve done is enhance their strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T01:15:51-08:00","id":1188434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188432#post1188432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were QKs in other Orders. The Orders killed them too. The reasons for this are very similar to the reasons in 1st edition, and no QK was going to be allowed to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aeon Preview #3, pg 8, end of paragraph #3 &quot;Dr. Bhurano also refused to allow quantakinetics to join other psi orders.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188432#post1188432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I disagree with your assertion that you\u2019re stuck with only one path for playing a QK. I know it\u2019s unfair that I have the benefit of having read what\u2019s coming, and can\u2019t just tell you all because of NDA ninjas, but soon you\u2019ll see why I disagree and we can discuss and explore the different ways together.</div> </div> </div> </div>You, as always, make a compelling case, and I guess I am going to have to wait, but the idea behind playing a QK interests me far more then I thought it would based on 1e experience. I also really like the various orders and, at least for the moment, I have to choose between playing a QK, or playing a member of any Order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188432#post1188432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But until you\u2019ve seen the QK powers, please don\u2019t assume that it\u2019s easy to tell that a quantakinetic isn\u2019t another psion, any more than you can spot the difference between a biokinetic and a vitakinetic if all they\u2019ve done is enhance their strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. However, according to the fiction piece Psions can... meld... join... something... where they can use each others Aptitudes to enhance their own. Once you do that with another, isn't it kind of obvious to them what type of Psion you are based on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T01:34:53-08:00","id":1188435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188434#post1188434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aeon Preview #3, pg 8, end of paragraph #3 &quot;Dr. Bhurano also refused to allow quantakinetics to join other psi orders.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I concede that point. Apologies for my missing it.<br /> <br /> The \u2018resurrection of the Chibs\u2019 Campaign pathways open up potential for more cross Order playing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T02:31:40-08:00","id":1188442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188435#post1188435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I concede that point. Apologies for my missing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't be quite so bad if the proceeding sentence hadn't been saying &quot;all of whom were scientists in a wide variety of fields, from physics to psychology&quot; Which seems to limit what Role you can choose to play down to Medical Practitioner and Technology Expert., assuming that you are one of the last few surviving QK's out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188435#post1188435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The \u2018resurrection of the Chibs\u2019 Campaign pathways open up potential for more cross Order playing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I very much look forward to reading the ideas presented for just such a campaign. I just hope that it is written from a very... player forward... mindset. (For example, if one of the players has a QK character, the option is available for them to become a new Proxy, and found their own order of QK's, rather then a &quot;Find NPC (X) and do fetch quests (A-G) and they will rebuild the CB, and give you an atta boy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: The later option can be good if the players don't have a QK in their group, but the option to found your own Order, rather then simply helping someone else rebuild the image shattered CB, would be a powerful hook for a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 02-22-2018, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T03:11:25-08:00","id":1188444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188442#post1188442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wouldn't be quite so bad if the proceeding sentence hadn't been saying &quot;all of whom were scientists in a wide variety of fields, from physics to psychology&quot; Which seems to limit what Role you can choose to play down to Medical Practitioner and Technology Expert., assuming that you are one of the last few surviving QK's out there.<br /> <br /> I very much look forward to reading the ideas presented for just such a campaign. I just hope that it is written from a very... player forward... mindset. (For example, if one of the players has a QK character, the option is available for them to become a new Proxy, and found their own order of QK's, rather then a &quot;Find NPC (X) and do fetch quests (A-G) and they will rebuild the CB, and give you an atta boy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: The later option can be good if the players don't have a QK in their group, but the option to found your own Order, rather then simply helping someone else rebuild the image shattered CB, would be a powerful hook for a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, any campaign built around the idea of creating your own Prometheus Chamber (Which would be required to found <i>any</i> Order, but especially for anyone trying to bring by the QKs) would be awesome. I'd love to have some ideas as to what the players would need to do to make that work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T03:19:19-08:00","id":1188447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188444#post1188444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, any campaign built around the idea of creating your own Prometheus Chamber (Which would be required to found <i>any</i> Order, but especially for anyone trying to bring by the QKs) would be awesome. I'd love to have some ideas as to what the players would need to do to make that work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating the Chamber is only the first part, you then have to found, recruit, fund, protect, organize, and network, your new Order. All of which can be just as difficult as creating/finding/guarding the Chamber in the first place. But I agree, any ideas about how players might go about creating a Prometheus Chamber would be amazing. Even if it has nothing to do with QK, a mythical home brewed 9th Aptitude, or a recreation of another Chamber for... purposes... could be a really fun premise for a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T03:33:17-08:00","id":1188449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188447#post1188447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating the Chamber is only the first part, you then have to found, recruit, fund, protect, organize, and network, your new Order. All of which can be just as difficult as creating/finding/guarding the Chamber in the first place. But I agree, any ideas about how players might go about creating a Prometheus Chamber would be amazing. Even if it has nothing to do with QK, a mythical home brewed 9th Aptitude, or a recreation of another Chamber for... purposes... could be a really fun premise for a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>The social side of it is relatively straight-forward - It's no different, really, than setting up a megacorp, or a country. Relatively &quot;simple&quot;, just really, really difficult. I'd be relatively confident running a game for that, just out of what we've already had previewed. <br /> <br /> But the Prometheus Chamber starts getting into the nitty-gritty setting details. I'd be less confident running that because there probably <i>is</i> a hard answer for how these things work, and it might be answered someday. <br /> <br /> For example, are Modes and Aptitudes definitively linked? Or could a new Chamber create a new Aptitude by recombining Modes? It's not inconceivable to pull Electrokinesis, Thermokinesis and either Photokinesis or Energetics into a single Aptitude, focused entirely on energy. The various Bio- &amp; Vitakinetic Modes can be combined in a few different ways. Telepathy and Clairsentience could cross over thematically. <br /> <br /> What exactly went differently for the Proxies? Because if you could turboboost a Prometheus Chamber so everyone came out at the Proxy level from the start, you've got a very different setting, very quickly. <br /> <br /> ... Basically, I'm ready for the Setting Secrets chapter. I can't wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T03:41:08-08:00","id":1188450,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that a Prometheus Chamber is the textbook example of a Wondrous Item. So we know the rules if we want to, and the SG allows one to, start with a Chamber. The problem is, we have no rules that cover how to make Wondrous Items, assuming that non-Nova's can even do so. If we did, it would be easy enough to wing that portion of making your own Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T03:46:13-08:00","id":1188452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188449#post1188449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, are Modes and Aptitudes definitively linked?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just flagging this one as something for us to discuss in a few days...<br /> <br /> I have opinions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T06:04:20-08:00","id":1188477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188452#post1188452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just flagging this one as something for us to discuss in a few days...<br /> <br /> I have opinions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll definitely look forward to that. If nothing else, it'll have a lot to say with regards to Psiads, I imagine (At some point, I'm going to run a stealth Psiad game. Probably Trinity era, working for Project Pandora. I've got a lot of ideas)<br /> <br /> Unrelated, but can you have multiple Auxiliary Modes? Because the rules read like you can, but the description of an Auxiliary Mode is that it's the Mode you're most strongly latent in and you develop a single dot in it naturally not long after being dunked, if you're activated in another Aptitude. That sort of seems to imply that you can only have one and it should probably be picked up in character gen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T07:24:49-08:00","id":1188504,"title":"","content":"I'm saying nothing else about QKs until the whole book has been previewed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188477#post1188477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated, but can you have multiple Auxiliary Modes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T09:42:16-08:00","id":1188549,"title":"","content":"Concept for a 9th aptitude. Luck.<br /> One mode basically grants Talent Gifts temporarily<br /> Another allows in world probability hacking (think mage 1e entropy sphere)<br /> The last lets you muck around with at table rolls. 5 dots = why did you bring d12s to a Onyx Path game... Oh, ffffffff--","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T10:42:09-08:00","id":1188568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188428#post1188428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of what you\u2019re asking is whether people can wander around with portable scanning devices to randomly test members of the public for latency. In this case, in my mind I\u2019d say no. *But*, Clairsentients can pick up on strong latency without anyone being aware of what they\u2019re doing. But there aren\u2019t that many clears, and they have better things to be doing than scanning for strong patents all the time.<br /> <br /> Summary: Testing for latency is difficult (but not impossible) to do without the person noticing. Strong latents can be detected silently, if you have a clear who could be bothered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more wondering how hard it is on your average potential latent to get testing done and if in countries that have universal health care if general screening seem to happen(which Nihon does), if Corporations could have manditory screenings, or even do so secretly as part of other general tests(like drug tests).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 02-22-2018, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T13:48:39-08:00","id":1188648,"title":"","content":"If any of the writers are willing to chip in, I'm interested to know if QK will be in the PSI Power Rules section that will be released tomorrow, or if we will have to wait til Setting Secrets before we get to see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T15:27:20-08:00","id":1188682,"title":"","content":"They've said it's in the secrets chapter, so next thursday (3-1)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T15:47:41-08:00","id":1188683,"title":"","content":"They said that Setting Secrets is where the CB stuff, and options for integrating QK's into your campaign, and campaign ideas for reintroducing them are going to be found. Nothing has stated where their PSI power rules are going to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T22:15:22-08:00","id":1188779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188648#post1188648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any of the writers are willing to chip in, I'm interested to know if QK will be in the PSI Power Rules section that will be released tomorrow, or if we will have to wait til Setting Secrets before we get to see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware, it's in the psi chapter. John may have moved it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T02:30:23-08:00","id":1188809,"title":"","content":"And yes, based on the next preview I just downloaded, Quantakinesis is there. Enjoy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T02:38:59-08:00","id":1188810,"title":"","content":"Woohoo! Also, damn this one is meaty; nice! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T04:09:53-08:00","id":1188825,"title":"","content":"The latest backer-only Update contains a link to the fourth section of the <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b> rulebook, including Chapter 7: Psionics, and Chapter 8: Technology. Feel free to discuss below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T04:15:14-08:00","id":1188827,"title":"","content":"I love the powers. Perikinesis is still my favourite. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (And yay for certain other changes, too) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T04:16:49-08:00","id":1188829,"title":"","content":"Time zone differences mean I\u2019m heading off to bed soon. If you have any questions about psionics, I\u2019ll try and get you some answers in the morning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T05:24:41-08:00","id":1188842,"title":"","content":"I just got finished doing my read thru of the PSI Powers, and let me say, job well done once again. Every time I came to the next mode it was &quot;You can do what?!?!&quot; &quot;Wow!&quot; and &quot;I so need to have this&quot;. Lots of &quot;I didn't even think of using (X) that way before.. cool.&quot; I am very much looking forward to running/playing in this game.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, correct me if I'm wrong, but couldn't Association (Transmutation ***) be used to recreate/repair the QK Chamber assuming you were able to get even a few of it's parts together, and had a high enough PSI score? (Temporarily at least)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 02-23-2018, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T07:52:53-08:00","id":1188869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188842#post1188842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Also, correct me if I'm wrong, but couldn't Association (Transmutation ***) be used to recreate/repair the QK Chamber assuming you were able to get even a few of it's parts together, and had a high enough PSI score? (Temporarily at least)</div> </div> </div> </div>The power specifically says it's for &quot;non-living structure(s)&quot;. Prometheus Chambers are very sophisticated bioware, and so not subject to Association's effects.<br /> <br /> Even if it were able to affect living material, it might not be able to repair the full chamber: I see each chamber as more of a colony of separate pieces of biotech, the same way a Portuguese man o' war isn't a single creature, but a &quot;colonial organism&quot; made up of multiple related and integrated organisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T08:01:09-08:00","id":1188870,"title":"","content":"The 6th dot powers improve the other powers of a Mode. Does that include the 7th dot power? Do 7th dot powers even belong to a Mode? I suspect they a part of any Mode whose 6th dot power you have.<br /> <br /> I think you should add a comment to the Psi chapter (and perhaps add it to the table) that aberrants don't have a Psi trait.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4081-thomas-weinbrenner","name":"Thomas Weinbrenner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T08:08:25-08:00","id":1188874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188869#post1188869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power specifically says it's for &quot;non-living structure(s)&quot;. Prometheus Chambers are very sophisticated bioware, and so not subject to Association's effects.<br /> <br /> Even if it were able to affect living material, it might not be able to repair the full chamber: I see each chamber as more of a colony of separate pieces of biotech, the same way a Portuguese man o' war isn't a single creature, but a &quot;colonial organism&quot; made up of multiple related and integrated organisms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I forgot they are Bioware.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T08:32:33-08:00","id":1188880,"title":"","content":"I am pleased beyond all reasonable amounts that the Upeo Death Drop made it into the new edition. <br /> Quantakinesis is SUPER interesting, especially Energetics. Just a really fun sounding set of powers that i could see being all kinds of fun in a story. <br /> That being said, Clairsentience remains my favorite of all the aptitudes, and this version really does it justice. i love the writeup for psychometry. <br /> <br /> a well written game book should give you ideas for stories constantly, even while you read the rules, and thats something thats happened constantly while i read these previews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4941-cielago","name":"Cielago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4941_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T09:20:55-08:00","id":1188894,"title":"","content":"Just started reading it and I'm super excited, though I have a quick question that isn't 100% clear: when you are networked together, combining your powers, do all of your psionic powers get boosted and as a result get the surcharge, or can you pick and choose what gets boosted if you are trying to conserve Psi?<br /> <br /> Also, that QK Enhanced Effect. Hoo boy that is useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T09:36:52-08:00","id":1188900,"title":"","content":"Cross-posted:<br /> <br /> Under formatting, is Vitality meant to be Stamina?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T11:18:17-08:00","id":1188938,"title":"","content":"&quot;Combining Psionic Aptitudes&quot;<br /> <br /> - It is weird that only some effects for Secondary Aptitudes depend on the Psi trait and others don't. There is no difference if you are boosted by a beginning quantakinetic or by their Proxy.<br /> <br /> - If there are multiple Psions with the same Aptitude boosting you, are the effects cumulative? (So if there were 5 quantakinetics, you could add 5 times your Psi trait? That seems quite unbalanced.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4081-thomas-weinbrenner","name":"Thomas Weinbrenner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T12:56:11-08:00","id":1188967,"title":"","content":"The Leviathan entry indicates that they can piggyback Orgotek Scarabs, but make no mention of the large frigates. In 1e, Levianthans could jump with the much larger hardtech frigates, as well as the battleships and carriers from the technology manual.<br /> <br /> Is this an intentional change or errata?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:40:52-08:00","id":1188982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188938#post1188938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- If there are multiple Psions with the same Aptitude boosting you, are the effects cumulative?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You get access to the same boost, regardless of how many representatives of that Aptitude are part of the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:53:33-08:00","id":1188989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188870#post1188870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 6th dot powers improve the other powers of a Mode. Does that include the 7th dot power? Do 7th dot powers even belong to a Mode? I suspect they a part of any Mode whose 6th dot power you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and 7th dot powers don\u2019t belong to any Mode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:54:13-08:00","id":1188990,"title":"","content":"Important note: you don't boost yourself. So the &quot;perfect&quot; group would be 16 people, two from each Aptitude. That way everyone is getting access to every boost (once).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:59:17-08:00","id":1188997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188894#post1188894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just started reading it and I'm super excited, though I have a quick question that isn't 100% clear: when you are networked together, combining your powers, do all of your psionic powers get boosted and as a result get the surcharge, or can you pick and choose what gets boosted if you are trying to conserve Psi?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can\u2019t pick and choose, no. <br /> <br /> Combining powers through Network works the same as usual, just without the physical contact. You can be in a Network and not be combining powers. If you want to combine, the group has to spend a round harmonizing their noetic fields. Thereafter, every power use by everyone in the group gains the benefits and incurs the surcharge. Any member can choose to break the combination, which ends it for the whole group. If they want to combine again, they\u2019ll have to spend another round harmonizing.<br /> <br /> Ending power combining doesn\u2019t automatically end the Network.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T16:14:22-08:00","id":1189037,"title":"","content":"The Clairsentience power &quot;Omniscience&quot; seems a bit underwhelming for a five-dot power. If I'm reading it properly, it only affects the area within the user's Radius -- which, in the case of non-Proxies, will be Short at most (or Medium, with an extra Psi spent.) &quot;Total sensory awareness&quot; with a radius of only 30 meters doesn't really seem worth the cost, especially since it doesn't seem to have any mechanical benefits (and you have to spend a success in order to focus on specific details.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T17:54:34-08:00","id":1189060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188967#post1188967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Leviathan entry indicates that they can piggyback Orgotek Scarabs, but make no mention of the large frigates. In 1e, Levianthans could jump with the much larger hardtech frigates, as well as the battleships and carriers from the technology manual.<br /> <br /> Is this an intentional change or errata?</div> </div> </div> </div>Intentional change, but in the thread over on rpg.net it sounds like John is going to change it to allow Leviathans to jump 2 size 5 ships if they\u2019re docked to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:21:21-08:00","id":1189071,"title":"","content":"if you have one of the six dot Proxy tier powers to increase Scale and those same effects, can you spend more than 1 Psi to get each benefit? Can you purchase a single benefit this way multiple times?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:24:24-08:00","id":1189072,"title":"","content":"Are there any plans to introduce an optional free-form psionics system like the mechanics in the 1e Player's Guide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:35:33-08:00","id":1189075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189072#post1189072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any plans to introduce an optional free-form psionics system like the mechanics in the 1e Player's Guide?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can only presume that will be added later, but as the various orders specialize in training one general area of psi and all of it's variant fields, players will tend to be pretty robust in the order they chose.and I cannot imagine that many will want a free psion running about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T19:19:42-08:00","id":1189084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Precision Understanding<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Success allows the psion can to the target\u2019s specific bioelectrical reaction to situations. </div> </div> </div>I think you accidentally a word?<br /> <br /> What is this supposed to say? I can't quite work it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","user":"Jetstream","date":". 02-23-2018, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T20:16:45-08:00","id":1189098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1188989#post1188989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, and 7th dot powers don\u2019t belong to any Mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>The dice pool to use Psi powers is usually Psi+Mode. So for 7th dot powers you have a reduced dice pool?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4081-thomas-weinbrenner","name":"Thomas Weinbrenner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T20:34:24-08:00","id":1189101,"title":"","content":"I like the change they are goinng to do to Levithan show, I wa nt thgem to be able carry frigates and such. <br /> <br /> So I was wondering are the three Modes per Aptitude and one power per dot the only categories of power existing or could, in theory, new modes or dot powers exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T20:57:12-08:00","id":1189102,"title":"","content":"So they're still going with the notion that baselines have Psi 1. <br /> <br /> Do Talents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T21:06:24-08:00","id":1189104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189102#post1189102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they're still going with the notion that baselines have Psi 1.<br /> <br /> Do Talents?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While it's not mentioned, I believe those suffering from severe quantum flux diseases should have Psi of 0. It would help explain the insidiousness of the illnesses and their resistance to modern medicine and even psionic healing.<br /> <br /> As to whether Talens have Psi 1, page 81 of the manuscript appears to indicate they do have a Psi rating (or the equivalent),<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Formatting Bioware<br /> Most bioware can be formatted, a process where the user\u2019s DNA is bonded to the item, allowing the user to control it more precisely, and permitting the device to draw energy from the user. Formatting an item requires one hour, and can only be performed in specialized facilities which can be found in any city outside of Nippon, but rarely in small, isolated settlements. <b>Any character with a Psi of at least one</b> can format bioware, <b>including psions, neutrals, and Talents</b>. Formatted bioware has many benefits, including removing the necessity for nutrient injections, and usually providing the user with 1 Enhancement to operate it, or some other benefit specific to the item. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T21:44:54-08:00","id":1189111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189098#post1189098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The dice pool to use Psi powers is usually Psi+Mode. So for 7th dot powers you have a reduced dice pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. For the purposes of dice pool, the 7-dot powers count as their \u2018own\u2019 Mode. That is, 7 dice. (And since you need to be a Psi 7 proxy to get them, it means your dice pool will likely be 14.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T21:46:13-08:00","id":1189112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189102#post1189102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they're still going with the notion that baselines have Psi 1. <br /> <br /> Do Talents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not specifically mentioned, but yes. Talents don\u2019t rate any higher than baselines on Psi latency tests, which basically means they have Psi 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T21:48:12-08:00","id":1189113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189104#post1189104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's not mentioned, I believe those suffering from severe quantum flux diseases should have Psi of 0. It would help explain the insidiousness of the illnesses and their resistance to modern medicine and even psionic healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, still Psi 1. The disease might be wrecking these poor unfortunates, but their bodies and baseline Psi do try to fight back, however ineffectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T21:49:45-08:00","id":1189114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189072#post1189072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any plans to introduce an optional free-form psionics system like the mechanics in the 1e Player's Guide?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I\u2019m aware of. The current system is pretty flexible, without being free form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T21:53:37-08:00","id":1189115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189071#post1189071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you have one of the six dot Proxy tier powers to increase Scale and those same effects, can you spend more than 1 Psi to get each benefit? Can you purchase a single benefit this way multiple times?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can spend multiple Psi points to increase different aspects, or gain one of the other benefits, but can only gain each benefit once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T22:44:29-08:00","id":1189122,"title":"","content":"So a biokin with clone what happens if the origional dies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T23:27:44-08:00","id":1189133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189122#post1189122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a biokin with clone what happens if the origional dies?</div> </div> </div> </div>We\u2019ve deliberately left that undefined. I\u2019d suggest going one of the following four ways, depending on your campaign\u2019s needs:<br /> <br /> 1) All clones suddenly cease to exist.<br /> 2) All clones continue to survive, and live until they die. None can ever develop the Clone power.<br /> 3) All clones continue to survive, and the eldest clone gains the potential to develop the Clone power. (Note, I say potential to develop. It\u2019s not automatic, and if the biokinetic\u2019s eldest clone was deliberately created as much less powerful than the proxy, it\u2019s going to have a lot of power-development to do.)<br /> 4) All clones continue to survive, and the last existing clone gains the potential to develop the Clone power. Battle Royale with a bunch of duplicates who suddenly have a motive to kill one another, and whose biokinetic powers explicitly *do* affect each other. This could be delightfully inventive and nasty.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019d probably go with option 3, but needs may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T23:47:59-08:00","id":1189139,"title":"","content":"So one of my players who tends to be very good at finding holes in things pointed out Energetics level 4 and Strong nuclear force leads to a whole lot of problems. My initial thought was to say that the noetic pattern of a thing wouldn't allow a differentiation between the Strong Nuclear force of a thing and the thing itself thus meaning it generally can't be messed with on that level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:27:24-08:00","id":1189163,"title":"","content":"I don`t played the Trinity Aeon in the first edition, I am knowing now this amazing setting, but I played Aberrant first edition.<br /> <br /> I don`t know how was the situation in 1st edition, but in Trinity Era new Novas/Aberrant still born/erupting in Earth and Colonies? If the answer is &quot;yes&quot; how the legal system, or military forces, deal with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:35:55-08:00","id":1189168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189163#post1189163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don`t played the Trinity Aeon in the first edition, I am knowing now this amazing setting, but I played Aberrant first edition.<br /> <br /> I don`t know how was the situation in 1st edition, but in Trinity Era new Novas/Aberrant still born/erupting in Earth and Colonies? If the answer is &quot;yes&quot; how the legal system, or military forces, deal with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>They kill them on sight, hunt down rumors of them when they can't see them, and search for them when the rumors become enough to warrant it. They treat them like the USA treats terrorists on the most wanted list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:39:24-08:00","id":1189178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189168#post1189168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They kill them on sight, hunt down rumors of them when they can't see them, and search for them when the rumors become enough to warrant it. They treat them like the USA treats terrorists on the most wanted list.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to Aberrants, anyway.<br /> <br /> The Novas of Eden, a group mostly untouched by Corruption who claim to want to help humanity, are kept under planetary quarantine as the power players figure out what to do about them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:54:26-08:00","id":1189185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189163#post1189163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but in Trinity Era new Novas/Aberrant still born/erupting in Earth and Colonies? If the answer is &amp;quot;yes&amp;quot; how the legal system, or military forces, deal with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but not very often, and vanishingly rare outside certain areas.<br /> <br /> As per Aberrant, Quantum eruptions are more likely to occur in a high-Quantum environment. As per AEon/Trinity, Psi and Quantum powers are antithetical to each other. Most of the small number of Aberrants will erupt in or near corruption zones. They\u2019re already unlikely to erupt in normal, baseline human society, and the presence of so many Psi-rich psions moving around the place now makes the environment downright hostile for Quantum events to occur at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:58:45-08:00","id":1189188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189185#post1189185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but not very often, and vanishingly rare outside certain areas.<br /> <br /> As per Aberrant, Quantum eruptions are more likely to occur in a high-Quantum environment. As per AEon/Trinity, Psi and Quantum powers are antithetical to each other. Most of the small number of Aberrants will erupt in or near corruption zones. They\u2019re already unlikely to erupt in normal, baseline human society, and the presence of so many Psi-rich psions moving around the place now makes the environment downright hostile for Quantum events to occur at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If only there were a a hightech nation that actively supresses psi of some sort that had something to hide.. oh well..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T05:16:23-08:00","id":1189199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189185#post1189185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but not very often, and vanishingly rare outside certain areas.<br /> <br /> As per Aberrant, Quantum eruptions are more likely to occur in a high-Quantum environment. As per AEon/Trinity, Psi and Quantum powers are antithetical to each other. Most of the small number of Aberrants will erupt in or near corruption zones. They\u2019re already unlikely to erupt in normal, baseline human society, and the presence of so many Psi-rich psions moving around the place now makes the environment downright hostile for Quantum events to occur at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Bunyip!<br /> <br /> Hum... This make Corruption Areas a top-priority to eliminate or restraing, but the Humanity don`t have the ways to eliminate yet.<br /> <br /> Another question about novas/aberrants: Humans have any genetic marker related to Nova? In part about Nippon, it is mentioned that public genetic treatment destroys psionic latency, what means the psionic have a genetic component, the same happens with Quantum potential?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T09:16:16-08:00","id":1189240,"title":"","content":"I cannot believe Biokinetics lets me be Ultimate Kars. I'm amazed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T08:37:20-08:00","id":1189407,"title":"","content":"Things, as I slowly finally get through preview 4.<br /> <br /> Posted on the kickstarter, but Telekinesis 3 - If you accelerate something to &quot;Supersonic&quot; speeds as an attack, it really shouldn't get the Silent tag for free. I can totally see being able to buy the silent tag, but if you kick a coin up to supersonic speeds, it still makes a sonic boom just like a bullet, it should still be as loud as a gun. <br /> <br /> Perikinesis. Very awesome power, I like the utility powers it gets as it advances. One thing. It says that it increases your armor rating, but never specifies if it's Hard or Soft armor. <br /> I can see several options.<br /> Examples assume PK 1 power with 2 mode dots.<br /> 1&gt; Always Soft armor - +2 soft armor<br /> 2&gt; Always Hard armor - +2 hard armor<br /> 3&gt; You can choose, possibly splitting - +2 soft armor OR +2 hard armor OR +1 soft and +1 hard<br /> 4&gt; It does both at once - +2 hard AND +2 soft armor.<br /> My assumption is the intended is #1, but I can easily see people making a different assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T08:49:28-08:00","id":1189411,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Biokinesis - How many dots in which modes would I need (minimum) to change my skin and eyes to unnatural colors, and grow non-functional aesthetic horns?<br /> Could I do this with Psychomorphing 1 and Transmogrify 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T09:54:24-08:00","id":1189421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189407#post1189407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perikinesis. Very awesome power, I like the utility powers it gets as it advances. One thing. It says that it increases your armor rating, but never specifies if it's Hard or Soft armor.<br /> I can see several options.<br /> Examples assume PK 1 power with 2 mode dots.<br /> 1&gt; Always Soft armor - +2 soft armor<br /> 2&gt; Always Hard armor - +2 hard armor<br /> 3&gt; You can choose, possibly splitting - +2 soft armor OR +2 hard armor OR +1 soft and +1 hard<br /> 4&gt; It does both at once - +2 hard AND +2 soft armor.<br /> My assumption is the intended is #1, but I can easily see people making a different assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?822666-Regarding-The-Trinity-Continuum&amp;p=21718190#post21718190\" target=\"_blank\">Perikinesis is always Soft Armor, per John Snead over on RPG.net.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T19:09:50-08:00","id":1189510,"title":"","content":"So, I've been looking for this rule for quite a while, and I can't seem to find it. How many dice do you roll when activating a Basic Power? It's easy enough for me to assume that you use your highest Mode in that Aptitude + PSI, but it never actually comes right out and says that, so it might be just PSI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T19:28:28-08:00","id":1189512,"title":"","content":"What are the differences between Quantum Flux areas that are corrupted and those that aren't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T23:16:15-08:00","id":1189537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189510#post1189510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been looking for this rule for quite a while, and I can't seem to find it. How many dice do you roll when activating a Basic Power? It's easy enough for me to assume that you use your highest Mode in that Aptitude + PSI, but it never actually comes right out and says that, so it might be just PSI.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it\u2019s highest Mode + Psi. I thought it was in there, but can\u2019t find it right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T00:13:49-08:00","id":1189547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189537#post1189537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it\u2019s highest Mode + Psi. I thought it was in there, but can\u2019t find it right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your reply, and good luck finding it. I've been combing thru the PDF all weekend, meticulously looking for it, and I've come up empty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T05:16:48-08:00","id":1189578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189512#post1189512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the differences between Quantum Flux areas that are corrupted and those that aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Areas that have flux, as described in the Trinity Continuum core, are like ripples in the surface of a pond. They're detectable but otherwise generally have little effect.<br /> <br /> Quantum Flux Zones as described in \u00c6on are like someone has dropped a big rock into the pond and stirred up all the mud from the bottom. The splash gets everything around it wet, and you don't want to drink the water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T06:13:59-08:00","id":1189583,"title":"","content":"Page 9 of the preview, in the little offset paragraph titled &quot;Psionic Dice Pools and Cost&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","user":"ffanxii4ever","date":". 02-26-2018, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T09:43:00-08:00","id":1189609,"title":"","content":"So would the wackness stirred up by Divis Mal back in the day that resulted in the huge wave of nova eruptions just be a massive regular area of flux, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T11:57:59-08:00","id":1189647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189583#post1189583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 9 of the preview, in the little offset paragraph titled &amp;quot;Psionic Dice Pools and Cost&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I knew it was in there, somewhere. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T14:47:32-08:00","id":1189701,"title":"","content":"I am little confused about Skill Trick, Psions, and Character Creation. In the CORE book it states that character do not start with Skill Tricks, but in Psion it states they do. One could assume that Psions do get Skill Tricks at character creation. However, since most of the rules for Psion character creation come from Continuum book I was wonder if this was just a miss-type/error. Direct clarification would be great. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T15:17:37-08:00","id":1189708,"title":"","content":"How do Psion's interact with Enhanced Edges? Namely Indomitable, it requires you to spend Inspiration to get its full effect and Psions do not posses that pool of resources. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T15:22:07-08:00","id":1189710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189701#post1189701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am little confused about Skill Trick, Psions, and Character Creation. In the CORE book it states that character do not start with Skill Tricks, but in Psion it states they do. One could assume that Psions do get Skill Tricks at character creation. However, since most of the rules for Psion character creation come from Continuum book I was wonder if this was just a miss-type/error. Direct clarification would be great. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I'm understanding correctly the <i>Aeon</i> reference is in error and nobody starts with Skill Tricks, they're always bought with experience. But I don't remember where I saw that clarification.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T07:13:26-08:00","id":1189856,"title":"","content":"The latest backer-only Update contains a link to the fifth section of the <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b> rulebook, including Chapter 9: Storyguide Advice, and Chapter 10: Opponents &amp; Allies. Feel free to discuss below.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T11:03:24-08:00","id":1189936,"title":"","content":"Is the last part going to come out or will we have to wait for the official release to see the setting secrets chapter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T11:24:00-08:00","id":1189950,"title":"","content":"They have said setting secrets will be released during the Kickstarter. The last day, I think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T15:15:46-08:00","id":1190021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189936#post1189936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the last part going to come out or will we have to wait for the official release to see the setting secrets chapter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Will be posted on Thursday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T16:50:53-08:00","id":1190060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1189701#post1189701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am little confused about Skill Trick, Psions, and Character Creation. In the CORE book it states that character do not start with Skill Tricks, but in Psion it states they do. One could assume that Psions do get Skill Tricks at character creation. However, since most of the rules for Psion character creation come from Continuum book I was wonder if this was just a miss-type/error. Direct clarification would be great. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe ruleset was still evolving while I was writing the Aeon chargen, and continued to do so after my drafts were done, so it looks like there's some rationalisation of the changes across all drafts that still needs to be performed - I'm assuming that will happen after the KS has concluded when the drafts go off for their remaining amendments and editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T07:47:17-08:00","id":1190666,"title":"","content":"The latest backer-only Update contains a link to the fifth section of the <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b> rulebook, including Chapter 11: Setting Secrets. Feel free to discuss below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T08:04:50-08:00","id":1190671,"title":"","content":"So if I'm reading this correctly, Superiors are in fact a new name for Stalwarts, and Nippon is secretly a Quantum-oriented powerhouse on Earth. <br /> <br /> The Venezuela Event will not happen for another century or so, if it happens at all; and it may not originate in Venezuela or possibly even in the Solar System if it <i>does</i> happen. It probably will happen though, kicking off the next era mentioned at the end of the Future History section the way the Hammersmith, Divas Mal, and Bhurano pulses kicked off the Adventure, Aberrant, and \u00c6on eras, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T08:30:23-08:00","id":1190675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1190671#post1190671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I'm reading this correctly, Superiors are in fact a new name for Stalwarts</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh. Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Superiors are an artificially-created type of eximorph. The naturally-occurring thing they most closely resemble is Adventure!'s stalwarts, but that's not a 1:1 association, any more than psiads and psions are the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Venezuela Event will not happen for another century or so, if it happens at all </div> </div> </div>There's no Venezuelan Phenomenon this time around. There's no need within the Aeon timeframe, since the 2104 event takes care of that.<br /> <br /> And after Aeon... well, arguably there's no need for any further Hammersmith events, as humanity will have a finer grasp on its own destiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T08:38:40-08:00","id":1190678,"title":"","content":"So the Melancholy of Transcendent Talents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T11:58:30-08:00","id":1190733,"title":"","content":"Close, but I'd say that it's more likely for the central character to be an unknowing Nova with Universe Creation. But yeah; you've got aliens, espers, and (the potential for) time travelers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T12:09:59-08:00","id":1190737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1190675#post1190675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no Venezuelan Phenomenon this time around. There's no need within the Aeon timeframe, since the 2104 event takes care of that.<br /> <br /> And after Aeon... well, arguably there's no need for any further Hammersmith events, as humanity will have a finer grasp on its own destiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm\u2026 there <i>is</i> still one reason I can think of to have it: it set up a very nice \u201ctime barrier\u201d that would allow you to put strong constraints on any time travelers from after the barrier who wish to visit times before the barrier while still letting them potentially go gonzo in the times after the barrier. That is, if you ever decide to give us a setting with Hyper-Talents who can time travel. <br /> <br /> What happens when mankind's destiny decides to come calling, literally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:28:54-08:00","id":1190768,"title":"","content":"The reveals and ideas in this chapter are great. Including the history background, how the proxies came about, and the Doyn menace. Oh by the way f them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In comment to comments above, I never really liked the time barrier so I'm fine with other reasons begin given for the Superiors. (Not that there is anythijng wrong with a time barrier, it has it's place.)<br /> <br /> I did wonder though do we ever learn who the Colony is. Is he an Aberrant War era nova or something else. I'm curious on that. <br /> <br /> Also is he one entity controlling millions others or are there multiple individuals inside the Colony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:02:33-08:00","id":1190780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1190768#post1190768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did wonder though do we ever learn who the Colony is. Is he an Aberrant War era nova or something else. I'm curious on that.<br /> <br /> Also is he one entity controlling millions others or are there multiple individuals inside the Colony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great questions. My guess, based on nothing but speculation, is it's name is a big clue. Like it started out in a colony of aberrants that went off into deep space to create a new world and a new life, and collapsed into a powerful hivemind. If that's something we already know to be true, pardon me. I don't remember a lot of old stuff and I haven't caught up on my reading.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see Colony be a featured threat in an adventure series.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:07:58-08:00","id":1190783,"title":"","content":"Back in the day lots of people liked Sin-Eater or Anibal Buendia (might be mispelled, the guy who created Eufiber) as potential origins for the Colony.<br /> <br /> Personally I kind of like the mystery. Every GM can decide individually. Maybe the Colony was nobody we've heard of, even!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:12:22-08:00","id":1190787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Topher Gerkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1190783#post1190783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in the day lots of people liked Sin-Eater or Anibal Buendia (might be mispelled, the guy who created Eufiber) as potential origins for the Colony.<br /> <br /> Personally I kind of like the mystery. Every GM can decide individually. Maybe the Colony was nobody we've heard of, even!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That works too. Mystery or no, I'd love to see it put into action. I liked that the Aeon line had actual adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T15:12:33-08:00","id":1190813,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that Colony wasn\u2019t someone significant in the Aberrant era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T17:27:43-08:00","id":1190859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1190813#post1190813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that Colony wasn\u2019t someone significant in the Aberrant era.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went in the exact opposite direction. I made it Alejandra, the pop star. Going from beloved by billions to hated freak is more then it would take to make anyone snap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T02:17:20-08:00","id":1190929,"title":"","content":"So what's the Venezuela event? Something mentioned as probably going to happen in 1st ed, like fulminating Quantum in a corrupted Zone about to start a New Nova age or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T05:14:40-08:00","id":1190949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1190929#post1190929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the Venezuela event? Something mentioned as probably going to happen in 1st ed, like fulminating Quantum in a corrupted Zone about to start a New Nova age or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's described in vague detail in Terra Verde, and certain aspects of it (like the exact cause) were left up to Storytellers to customize for their games. But the gist is that something weird happens in a Nor\u00e7a lab, and it causes something like the Hammersmith explosion. Daredevils/Talents appear in substantial (for them) numbers, as do naturally-occurring psychics (psiads). There are also eruptions of low-power/low-Taint novas (or possibly just Stalwarts, or likely both) and full-blown heavily-mutated aberrants. In addition, existing psions' abilities are either increased or decreased in seemingly-random ways. The clairsentients, while not knowing exactly what would happen, knew something was up because they couldn't see into the future past that point because of the noetic interference (and afterwards, can't see back into the past before it).<br /> <br /> And it all makes a little more sense when you keep in mind that (IIRC) the book was supposed to come out at the same time as Adventure!, for a bit of thematic synergy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T09:13:03-08:00","id":1191007,"title":"","content":"The details of the Venezuelan Phenomenon were as follows:<br /> <br /> Proxy del Fuego is capable of producing biokinetic clones. One of these clones was checking in on a top-secret Nor\u00e7a lab in one of the Venezuelan quarantine zones: a lab that happened to employ most/all of the quantakinetics del Fuego had rescued. The ambient Taint in the quarantine zone masked their presence.<br /> <br /> Among the lab's research was the discovery that psions could be possessed by Doyen. Del Fuego kind of panicked, because he realized he couldn't trust anyone, <i>including himself</i> (or to be more accurate, Del Fuego Prime or any of his other clones). So he had the quantakinetics destroy the lab in such a way that it would look like an Aberrant attack (and read that way to any noetic detection). He went into hiding with them. Del Fuego Prime knows that his clone is still alive, but figures there's a good reason he hasn't returned home yet.<br /> <br /> Del Fuego was also working on an updated version of some old plans he'd come across for a sort of unlimited energy device, something called a Hammersmith engine. Just like Elon Musk is distributing a satellite network to provide internet access to the world, Del Fuego wanted to do the same with distribution of energy. His clone, however, triggered them prematurely, hoping that the subquantum &quot;static&quot; they generated would keep any Doyen away from Earth. Dozens of satellites triggered Hammersmith events simultaneously.<br /> <br /> On the upside, it worked: any Doyen on Earth were effectively booted out. On the other hand, things got weird. Daredevils manifested, psiads started popping up, even some low-powered and unTainted Aberrants<br /> .<br /> That was the Venezuelan Phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T19:11:03-08:00","id":1191197,"title":"","content":"Do the Lunar and Martian states, orbital stations, and human starships of Aeon have artificial gravity. Maybe I missed it but I don't see grav crystals or the like mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T19:13:16-08:00","id":1191200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191197#post1191197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Lunar and Martian states, orbital stations, and human starships of Aeon have artificial gravity. Maybe I missed it but I don't see grav crystals or the like mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, grav crystals for artificial gravity are near-standard use in ships and stations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T19:44:39-08:00","id":1191212,"title":"","content":"Thanks Bunyip. Do you by any chance know what section it might be in. I'm interested in reading what's written, even if it's a paragraph. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T20:00:03-08:00","id":1191214,"title":"","content":"I can't help but think a perfect spoiler idea would be about Eden. Where you guys say nothing sinister is going on, the Novas are not corrupted or monstrous, and no mental manipulation has ever been done on the baselines. That things are exactly what they seem and the Novas and baselines do actually have good lives. <br /> <br /> I mean I know it's not necessary but I think it would be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T20:48:57-08:00","id":1191221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191212#post1191212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Bunyip. Do you by any chance know what section it might be in. I'm interested in reading what's written, even if it's a paragraph. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As I look through now, I think the actual entry for grav crystals under tech may have been trimmed for space.<br /> <br /> What we still have talks about their utility, but doesn\u2019t specifically define them.<br /> <br /> AEon preview 1, p48 (last sentence on the page) - \u2018The best use grav crystals...\u2019<br /> AEon preview 2, p8 (Lor Gravity Adaptation) - \u2018Although grav grids are common...\u2019<br /> p9 (Mars) - \u2018large pressurized cities equipped with grav grids...\u2019<br /> AEon preview 5, p23 \u2018Chromatic technology does not include grav crystals...\u2019<br /> <br /> Edit to add: And they\u2019re included in the glossary in preview 1. Don\u2019t know why that didn\u2019t show up on my search, but they are defined.<br /> <br /> \u201cGrav Crystals: Nova age technology that can create stable artificial gravity over large areas. \u201c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 03-02-2018, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T21:17:25-08:00","id":1191230,"title":"","content":"Thank you. You are the best. I really appreciate that. <br /> <br /> I like how it's specifically nova tech, which is cool because it shows they are not destroying understandable technology. And I like that. <br /> <br /> Though may I say that an entry in the tech section could be useful. Heck 1e trinity got a whole huge sidebar (Which was more than needed to be honest, lol). <br /> <br /> But really, thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T22:39:52-08:00","id":1191257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191007#post1191007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The details of the Venezuelan Phenomenon were as follows:<br /> <br /> Proxy del Fuego is capable of producing biokinetic clones. One of these clones was checking in on a top-secret Nor\u00e7a lab in one of the Venezuelan quarantine zones: a lab that happened to employ most/all of the quantakinetics del Fuego had rescued. The ambient Taint in the quarantine zone masked their presence.<br /> <br /> Among the lab's research was the discovery that psions could be possessed by Doyen. Del Fuego kind of panicked, because he realized he couldn't trust anyone, <i>including himself</i> (or to be more accurate, Del Fuego Prime or any of his other clones). So he had the quantakinetics destroy the lab in such a way that it would look like an Aberrant attack (and read that way to any noetic detection). He went into hiding with them. Del Fuego Prime knows that his clone is still alive, but figures there's a good reason he hasn't returned home yet.<br /> <br /> Del Fuego was also working on an updated version of some old plans he'd come across for a sort of unlimited energy device, something called a Hammersmith engine. Just like Elon Musk is distributing a satellite network to provide internet access to the world, Del Fuego wanted to do the same with distribution of energy. His clone, however, triggered them prematurely, hoping that the subquantum &quot;static&quot; they generated would keep any Doyen away from Earth. Dozens of satellites triggered Hammersmith events simultaneously.<br /> <br /> On the upside, it worked: any Doyen on Earth were effectively booted out. On the other hand, things got weird. Daredevils manifested, psiads started popping up, even some low-powered and unTainted Aberrants<br /> .<br /> That was the Venezuelan Phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, while it may not be needed to create a &quot;temporal&quot; barrier, I wonder if the basic idea will be modified for allowing Psiads to appear in the setting in significant numbers. As of the setting right now, there are no known Psiads... and even the Secrets section doesn't mention there being any... save the possibility that Proxy Bhurano might have become one had her psychic powers hadn't been castrated by the Doyen to limit her growth and potential.<br /> <br /> At the moment, it seems that unless such an event happens, the chances of Psiads developing in the current setting seems remote (maybe after the limitations imposed by the Doyen and their Prometheus Chambers have been eliminated/corrected).<br /> <br /> Still... given what we do know about Del Fuego in 2E, he does seem convinced that whatever the Doyen did to unlock the psychic potential in both the Proxies and the Psions in general, it also imposed limitations to their power... limitations that Del Fuego seems intent on eliminating.<br /> <br /> As for having it produce more Talents, Novas and such... it is also possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T23:30:09-08:00","id":1191268,"title":"","content":"Didn't the secrets section have Bhurano's powers awakened by the Hammersmith experiment in the 20s? That would make her a psiad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T00:23:40-08:00","id":1191278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191257#post1191257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are no known Psiads...</div> </div> </div> </div>As the setting stands right now, that\u2019s apparently correct, but since we hit that stretch goal, who knows what will be?<br /> <br /> Plus, just because Project Pandora hasn\u2019t publicly disclosed anything, doesn\u2019t mean they haven\u2019t found anything...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191257#post1191257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and even the Secrets section doesn't mention there being any... save the possibility that Proxy Bhurano might have become one had her psychic powers hadn't been castrated by the Doyen to limit her growth and potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019ve misinterpreted that. Bhurano was a psiad - the Doyen forced her to become a psion so they could study QK and control her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T09:08:44-08:00","id":1191362,"title":"","content":"I look forward to seeing some fun character dynamics between Bhurano, Mercer, and Donigal/Mal in Adventure! and Aberrant material.<br /> <br /> While I know extradiagetically it\u2019s a change between editions, I can totally buy the in-universe documents in first edition failing to mention Bhurano at the Hammersmith event because to the white gentlemen adventurers present and journalists covering the story she was basically part of Hammersmith furniture set and they forgot her when accounting for where everyone was at the event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T09:51:02-08:00","id":1191369,"title":"","content":"Every good gentleman of fine breeding and sophistication knows that psiad women should be seen and not heard.<br /> <br /> <br /> /sarc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T10:58:53-08:00","id":1191393,"title":"","content":"Another quick question. More a potential for the future. <br /> <br /> But can additional Modes potentially exist. I guess is this a potential space for future development or is three Modes per Aptitude all there is. <br /> <br /> Also can additional powers exist per dot level. Can a second 3-dot power exist thst needs to be purchased. <br /> <br /> I'm not so much asking if you guys made such things (as 8 aptitudes x three Modes each x 7 powers per mode is not a small amount) bit if as a theoretical design space they might occur. <br /> <br /> The reason I am asking is iblik e the idea of specialized powers and unique modes having the potential to exist. <br /> <br /> As a note I might have asked this but I have posted a lot of questions since the kickstarter began so it's hard to double check. <br /> <br /> Oh, as a note, I like how the merit analogs can modify certain powers. Like the QK society one modifying there ability to hide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T11:32:40-08:00","id":1191402,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Adventure! fluff needs to change in any way from 1E. The setting material doesn't need an update to incorporate time passed like Aberrant will; it's still the 1920s<i>. </i>They could just resuse the old setting chapter, with minimal changes if necessary. I'm curious what the devs' plan is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T12:36:56-08:00","id":1191417,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure there are no plans at the moment for additional modes or powers. As it stands, the existing modes are very flexible! Players and Storyguides can work together to determine what a given mode might or might not be able to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T13:09:13-08:00","id":1191428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191230#post1191230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how it's specifically nova tech, which is cool because it shows they are not destroying understandable technology. And I like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's true that not everything novas have created is destroyed, keep in mind that &quot;Nova Age technology&quot; isn't necessarily the same thing as &quot;nova technology.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T13:20:03-08:00","id":1191429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191402#post1191402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the Adventure! fluff needs to change in any way from 1E. The setting material doesn't need an update to incorporate time passed like Aberrant will; it's still the 1920s<i>. </i>They could just resuse the old setting chapter, with minimal changes if necessary. I'm curious what the devs' plan is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still the 1920s, but that doesn't mean the setting hasn't changed in order to better represent the Continuum we've got with this new edition. Sara Kaur's presence, for example, is a notable difference. So no, don't count on the setting chapter being copied-and-pasted any more than it was for Aeon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T13:40:57-08:00","id":1191438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191429#post1191429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's still the 1920s, but that doesn't mean the setting hasn't changed in order to better represent the Continuum we've got with this new edition. Sara Kaur's presence, for example, is a notable difference. So no, don't count on the setting chapter being copied-and-pasted any more than it was for Aeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>*cough*planetary-romance-supplement*cough*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T23:46:07-08:00","id":1191555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191278#post1191278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You\u2019ve misinterpreted that. Bhurano was a psiad - the Doyen forced her to become a psion so they could study QK and control her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much a misinterpretation as a choice not to make an assumption that wasn't specifically stated. Yes, it was said she gained vast psychic potential, but it was never actually stated that she was able to reach any notable level of it before the Doyen contacted her an the other would-be Proxies. Yes, there are a number of months between the setting off of the noetic device in early 2104 and the Doyen creating the 8 Proxies late that year, but would this be enough time for her to develop any of her psychic gifts beyond the most basic levels (even with a Psi rating of 3 or more) before the Doyen castrated that development to control her power? Maybe... but we may never know for sure how far she had progressed before she was possessed by the Doyen.<br /> <br /> Rereading the section, it does say that the noetic device she set off to reduce the various corrupted lands did indeed have the effect of creating hundreds of new Talents and Psiads around the world (and hundreds of thousands of Latents), so maybe a new event isn't needed. Why none of these individuals have surfaced is a question that will need to be answered when the Psiad rules come out. Chances are that many of them have been diagnosed as &quot;Latents&quot; and been subjected to the same awakening that creates Psions... similar to what happened to Proxy Bhurano (where her Psiad potential has been effectively castrated). As for what happens to those who decide they don't want to join a Psi-Order... it would depend on just how paranoid the Doyen are (and how closely they are paying attention to the identifying of &quot;Latents&quot;).<br /> <br /> Judging from their fear of Proxy Bhurano, chances are that they would be very concerned about any other naturally occuring Psiad emerging from humanity. If such an individual can be identified as more than just a mere Latent, chances are that the Doyen will arrange for some sort of surveillance of the individual, to see if they develop any powers at a later date. How long this surveillance lasts will depend on how determined the Doyen are to control any such potential threats (likely for a few years at least, given how paranoid these aliens seem to be). If the would-be Psiad begins to show signs of developing their powers outside of the Psi-Orders, I can see the Doyen responding in three ways.<br /> <br /> 1) Manipulate events around the Psiad that sees them put some place where they can be monitored more carefully. This can be anything from having them arrested for a crime, to having them committed... or even getting a dream job (or even finding a &quot;soul&quot; mate) where they can be watched closely by the Doyen or their agents very closely.<br /> <br /> 2) Arrange a situation that would make the Psiad reconsider joining one of the Psi-Orders (either by choice or by lack of any other choice) where their potential power can be curbed (forced to become a Psion with all the limitations that come with that).<br /> <br /> 3) Arrange an event that will eliminate the potential threat the Psiad might pose to the Doyen... though it seems unlikely the Doyen would lower themselves to anything this direct (too cowardly to eliminate a Psion directly as the risk of being discovered by the Psiad and possibly destroyed is too great, even if it is fairly slim).<br /> <br /> All of these could contribute to how rare identifiable Psiads seem to be. Of course we will know more once the Psiad rules are available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T00:52:31-08:00","id":1191566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191555#post1191555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much a misinterpretation as a choice not to make an assumption that wasn't specifically stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191555#post1191555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course we will know more once the Psiad rules are available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T05:34:15-08:00","id":1191600,"title":"","content":"So, in-universe question about Auxiliary Modes? <br /> <br /> Are they something that people can deliberately train? Like, if I'm really keen to get a single dot in Vitakinesis (Because, honestly, who wouldn't?) are there skills I can practice, mindsets I can train, or concepts I can meditate on in order to develop that Mode? Or are they <i>solely</i> natural offshoots of my Latency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T08:40:57-08:00","id":1191623,"title":"","content":"I may be misunderstanding the question, but as far as the book goes, Bhurano developed psychic powers at the original Hammersmith event in the 1920s and spent a century or two developing them before her Doyen-induced transformation into a psion. She didn't just suddenly develop powers when she set off her noetic beacon (although that was when she discovered Quantakinesis).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:05:42-08:00","id":1191628,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting is that Bhurano's burst caused the emergence of \u201chundreds of new Talents and psiads\u201d. While Psiads are a tiny minority in \u00c6on, they've already been established as existing, even before the stretch goal for them was achieved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:13:41-08:00","id":1191651,"title":"","content":"I'm really upset about Bhurano's because the Doyen basically noetically castrated her. She went from someone capable of learning great many powers to just one aptitude. It's so scream worthy. <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Great job writers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Ps. I totally want her to be able to push passed the Doyen manipulations yo regasin hee super Psiad nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:24:11-08:00","id":1191657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191651#post1191651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ps. I totally want her to be able to push passed the Doyen manipulations yo regasin hee super Psiad nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally something she's working on at my table - and potentially to liberate all Psions from their Doyen-imposed limitations - resulting in psychomorphs that will unite the flexibility of Psiads with the acheivable power heights of Psions as the new norm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T11:07:00-08:00","id":1191684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191651#post1191651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really upset about Bhurano's because the Doyen basically noetically castrated her. She went from someone capable of learning great many powers to just one aptitude. It's so scream worthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>She wasn't &quot;castrated.&quot; She doesn't have noetic testicles and she wasn't noetically having offspring. Plenty of more accurate words: Curtailed. Limited, Pared, Curbed, Restricted, Confined.<br /> <br /> It's irritating that Bhurano's potential was curtailed, but it's not like she hasn't had 200 years to learn different psi abilities. Quantakinesis aside, she's probably learned more psi powers than anyone in history. And she's in a better position to do something about the artificial limitations on Aptitude than anyone else. So yeah, it sucks, but it's not like she's been cut down to the level of a newly-dunked psion, or even to the level of most proxies. She probably has access to at least a dot or two from every Aptitude, and probably more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 03-04-2018, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T11:53:33-08:00","id":1191700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191684#post1191684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She wasn't &quot;castrated.&quot; She doesn't have noetic testicles and she wasn't noetically having offspring. Plenty of more accurate words: Curtailed. Limited, Pared, Curbed, Restricted, Confined.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Castrate&quot; seems fairly accurate, to deprive someone of an ability, often forcibly by others, to prevent development in a particular area. True, it usually has &quot;sexual&quot; connotations, but it still quite accurately describes what was forced upon Proxy Bhurano.<br /> <br /> While the Doyen couldn't alter any of the abilities she had before the noetic device was set off (such as longevity or her regenerative powers), the Secrets chapter is fairly clear that they were very capable of limiting her development of Psychic Abilities... especially since a Doyen Possessed her for 8 years (and likely didn't develop any of her abilities beyond what was needed to study Quantakinesis). How much she has developed in the 12 years she has been presumed dead remains to be seen, but even before she set off the device in 2104, she knew more about Quantum and Noetic powers than anyone (yet her device still had effects she didn't expect, suggesting that even she doesn't know everything about the subject... yet). It is unclear whether she had much in the way of Psychic power before her device was activated (the Secrets chapter suggests that her Psychic potential was greatly increased, but it is unclear if she had awakened as a Psiad before that or not).<br /> <br /> While I will admit that as a developer of the setting, you are in a much better position to know what Proxy Bhurano is capable of... and that she is likely the most powerful of the Proxies (beyond what most of the others would be capable of), but let's not shortchange the efforts the Doyen were able to do to curb her potential power. She may have 200 years of knowledge, but they have millions of years of dealing with other Noetically gifted species (and with getting others to destroy Quantum gifted species). True, the Doyen have never encountered a species quite as gifted as humans before... and if anyone can figure out how to undo the limitations they Doyen are imposing upon human Psions, it will likely be Proxy Bhurano (assuming of course she survives long enough to do so).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T12:55:23-08:00","id":1191720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191700#post1191700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Castrate&amp;quot; seems fairly accurate, to deprive someone of an ability, often forcibly by others, to prevent development in a particular area. True, it usually has &amp;quot;sexual&amp;quot; connotations, but it still quite accurately describes what was forced upon Proxy Bhurano.</div> </div> </div> </div>It specifically and precisely isn\u2019t accurate. It\u2019s a poor choice of word, when several, more accurate choices exist - as Ian noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191700#post1191700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I will admit that as a developer of the setting, you are in a much better position to know what Proxy Bhurano is capable of...</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it would be nice if you\u2019d accept that when we\u2019re engaging in discussion here, we\u2019re doing so in good faith. Your tactic of instant disagreement followed by lecturing us on what we already know discourages further engagement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T22:30:37-08:00","id":1191847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191720#post1191720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then it would be nice if you\u2019d accept that when we\u2019re engaging in discussion here, we\u2019re doing so in good faith. Your tactic of instant disagreement followed by lecturing us on what we already know discourages further engagement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken. Subject is dropped. No further engagement needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T23:01:48-08:00","id":1191851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191600#post1191600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in-universe question about Auxiliary Modes? <br /> <br /> Are they something that people can deliberately train? Like, if I'm really keen to get a single dot in Vitakinesis (Because, honestly, who wouldn't?) are there skills I can practice, mindsets I can train, or concepts I can meditate on in order to develop that Mode? Or are they <i>solely</i> natural offshoots of my Latency?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question, and one I don\u2019t believe has been addressed before. <br /> <br /> Speaking unofficially, my opinion would be that (in character) Auxiliary Modes are entirely offshoots of the psion\u2019s latency, and can\u2019t be \u2018trained\u2019 into developing. OOC, the player can choose whatever Auxialiary Modes they want, if they have the experience to spend.<br /> <br /> That said, when a psion enters proxy tier and can gain up to 2 dots in an Auxiliary Mode, I\u2019d say they can train their existing, \u2018spontaneous\u2019 Mode into the higher level, because they have something to build on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T17:40:45-08:00","id":1192096,"title":"","content":"If I wanted to hack into someone's Biocomp via psionics, would I use Electromanipulation or Technokinesis? If Electromanipulation, which power would I need? Because there doesn't seem to be a direct &quot;hack biotech&quot; set of powers, unlike the ones for Hard Tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T01:15:08-08:00","id":1192172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1192096#post1192096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wanted to hack into someone's Biocomp via psionics, would I use Electromanipulation or Technokinesis? If Electromanipulation, which power would I need? Because there doesn't seem to be a direct &amp;quot;hack biotech&amp;quot; set of powers, unlike the ones for Hard Tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Electromanipulation, with dots 2-5 being roughly equivalent to Technokinesis 1-4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T01:21:31-08:00","id":1192174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1191393#post1191393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another quick question. More a potential for the future. <br /> <br /> But can additional Modes potentially exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. In the sense that I don\u2019t believe there has been any conversation around it as yet.<br /> <br /> We tried to make the available powers as broad as possible, often giving several possible effects. The current set of powers also incorporates most things from the powers that appeared in 1e core, as well as the alternative powers from the sourcebooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T12:14:14-08:00","id":1193669,"title":"","content":"Hey Bunyip, thanks for the answer. I appreciate it. <br /> <br /> Random question, telepathy power Division. Can a Psion use it to create an artificial mind in a bioapp or computer or sonethunbg like that. <br /> <br /> So, byvthe way, I totally see the themes of the Babylon 5 PsiCorps in the telepathy powers. I like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T14:25:16-08:00","id":1193696,"title":"","content":"Would applying biokensis effects to other organisms (thus engineering new life forms/biotech) be something thematically out of range for Psions, and cutting into Eximorph mutant-making thematic space?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T14:43:34-08:00","id":1193707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1193696#post1193696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would applying biokensis effects to other organisms (thus engineering new life forms/biotech) be something thematically out of range for Psions, and cutting into Eximorph mutant-making thematic space?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen what combining aptitudes with Vitakinesis can do?<br /> <br /> I think you'd probably have to introduce some kind of narrative or edge factor to like, make the effect permanent or last longer, but biokinetics who combine aptitudes with vitakinetics can do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T14:46:48-08:00","id":1193709,"title":"","content":"You can\u2019t use Biokinesis on other organisms.<br /> <br /> You could pair with a vitakinetic to apply effects to other creatures, but this isn\u2019t engineering anything different, just altering shapes and abilities. It will fade unless you keep committing psi, and it\u2019s unlikely a biokinetic will want to waste their psi on just keeping altered \u2018pets\u2019.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T10:15:30-07:00","id":1194565,"title":"","content":"What's the publicly stated reason for Nippon's anti-psion/biotech policies? Because the gov has not informed the world or their citizenry about their alien tech discoveries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T23:02:48-07:00","id":1195980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1194565#post1194565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the publicly stated reason for Nippon's anti-psion/biotech policies? Because the gov has not informed the world or their citizenry about their alien tech discoveries.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Nipponese are a weird isolationist culture, who knows why they do anything?&quot; is what I've been assuming was the standard reason, but you make a good point that there would be smart people who would want an actual reason for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T23:19:01-07:00","id":1195981,"title":"","content":"I suppose a simple \u201cthe Orders that have a monopoly on the creation of Psions are inherently foreign interests, and thus the loyalties of all Psions must be treated as suspect\u201d suffices...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T05:53:06-07:00","id":1196023,"title":"","content":"\u201cLook what happened last time we blindly trusted super-powered beings...\u201d works for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:12:14-07:00","id":1196041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1193709#post1193709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can\u2019t use Biokinesis on other organisms.<br /> <br /> You could pair with a vitakinetic to apply effects to other creatures, but this isn\u2019t engineering anything different, just altering shapes and abilities. It will fade unless you keep committing psi, and it\u2019s unlikely a biokinetic will want to waste their psi on just keeping altered \u2018pets\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There goes psionically helping someone transition...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:15:02-07:00","id":1196043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1195981#post1195981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose a simple \u201cthe Orders that have a monopoly on the creation of Psions are inherently foreign interests, and thus the loyalties of all Psions must be treated as suspect\u201d suffices...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More cynical types might point to the nacient field of biotech is a field the Nipponese aren't a decade or so advanced on everyone else and that by promoting fear of this they keep their monopoly on Tech dominance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T08:23:01-07:00","id":1196068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1196041#post1196041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There goes psionically helping someone transition...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd definitely rule that medical biotech advances have that covered. Wouldn't be as simple as a biokinetic's ability to alter themselves at will, but it'd still be far more complete and easier than today for a trans person who wants to to change their sexual morphology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T08:44:20-07:00","id":1196076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1196041#post1196041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There goes psionically helping someone transition...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually called out as a specific use of Vitakinesis (five dots in Iatrosis, Adjust Template).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T20:33:14-07:00","id":1196344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1196041#post1196041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There goes psionically helping someone transition...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you could use the right tool for the job. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Topher Gerkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1196076#post1196076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually called out as a specific use of Vitakinesis (five dots in Iatrosis, Adjust Template).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T22:48:09-07:00","id":1198566,"title":"","content":"I don't see a Q&amp;A thread so I will ask here.<br /> <br /> It seems to me we are missing a Performance and Craft ability. Though it seems Technology can be used to repair and craft, its very emphasized that its more for electronics and such. And how do we do a Performance roll, like play the guitar, or do a fancy dance or Sing? Maybe an edge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T06:16:20-07:00","id":1198623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1198566#post1198566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see a Q&amp;A thread so I will ask here.<br /> <br /> It seems to me we are missing a Performance and Craft ability. Though it seems Technology can be used to repair and craft, its very emphasized that its more for electronics and such. And how do we do a Performance roll, like play the guitar, or do a fancy dance or Sing? Maybe an edge?</div> </div> </div> </div>To my understanding (and this applies to Scion too, so I would imagine it would apply to all Storypath games), you simply don't have a Craft or a Performance skill. Instead, one of your paths aligns appropriately (something like a Tinkerer or a Rock Star Path), and then what matters is the point of the roll? Are you trying to make people feel something? Presence+Empathy. Are you trying to show off your technical expertise while dancing? Dexterity+Athletics. Are you leading people to goal, like in any number of musicals? Presence+Command. Are you showcasing a specific And so on.<br /> <br /> For Craft, again, it matters what the relevant path is and then what you're crafting/repairing. If it is a beautiful portrait or sculpture, it would probably be Dexterity+Humanties, maybe Presence+Humanities for a particularly emotional piece. Are you building a quick-and-dirty shelter in the middle of the woods to keep you out of the rain? Intellect+Survival. Some sort of gadget? Intellect+Science or Technology to plan it, Cunning to jury-rig it, Dexterity if it volatile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T06:52:18-07:00","id":1198629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1198566#post1198566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see a Q&amp;A thread so I will ask here.<br /> <br /> It seems to me we are missing a Performance and Craft ability. Though it seems Technology can be used to repair and craft, its very emphasized that its more for electronics and such. And how do we do a Performance roll, like play the guitar, or do a fancy dance or Sing? Maybe an edge?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cArtistic Talent\u201d is a 1-3 point edge. You gain an Enhancement from the Edge toward the goal of your performance or creation (probably Persuasion, Command, Culture, or Larceny)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:25:13-07:00","id":1198769,"title":"","content":"So technically aren't the Doyen basically Psiads?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T17:10:09-07:00","id":1198897,"title":"","content":"Depends what you mean. If you define psiads as naturally-occurring psions, then you could say yes. If you define psiads as naturally-occurring human psions, no.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re using some other definition entirely, you\u2019ll have to let us know what you\u2019re thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T17:15:09-07:00","id":1198900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1198897#post1198897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you define psiads as naturally-occurring psions, then you could say yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Because to me that is what a Psiad is, a naturally occurring Psion. <br /> <br /> Well, really, we should more aptly say that a Psion is an artificial Psiad, but yeah. Hehe <br /> <br /> Thanks for the response. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T04:39:31-07:00","id":1199002,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you could call the Doyen psiads, though, even if you were using the broader definition of &quot;naturally occurring psion.&quot; Because they are extensively genetically engineered. They just stopped short of whatever the final stage of psi power happened to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1529-srgrvsalot","name":"SrGrvsaLot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T11:25:20-08:00","id":1271803,"title":"","content":"Ok I don't see this discussed anywhere else so I'm going to post it here. In the manuscript it says that a tesser can be added to any vessel of size 4 or greater that has the psi tag. By my read, that means an Orgotek Scarab frigate is valid and can run the tesser assuming it has the ARES pod. Is that a correct interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5930-deathchipmunk","name":"DeathChipmunk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T16:34:53-08:00","id":1273348,"title":"","content":"Alright, I know I'm super late on this, but this thread still seems like the best place for general questions. If the limit for teleportation jumps is within the same galaxy, how do jump ships cross lightyears of space? Do they do that in multiple jumps or does some part of the ship help them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T17:53:41-08:00","id":1273356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1273348#post1273348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I know I'm super late on this, but this thread still seems like the best place for general questions. If the limit for teleportation jumps is within the same galaxy, how do jump ships cross lightyears of space? Do they do that in multiple jumps or does some part of the ship help them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the Milky Way galaxy is 100,000 lightyears across, so they don't need to be able to cross the galactic border to travel lightyears. The next closest galaxy (full, not satelite) is Andromeda and it is 2.5 million lightyears away from Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T18:03:32-08:00","id":1273357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1273348#post1273348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I know I'm super late on this, but this thread still seems like the best place for general questions. If the limit for teleportation jumps is within the same galaxy, how do jump ships cross lightyears of space? Do they do that in multiple jumps or does some part of the ship help them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you confusing galaxies and solar systems? Interstellar jumps between solar systems cross light years of space within the same galaxy. Given the number of star systems in the Milky Way, I honestly can\u2019t imagine a narrative reason to move beyond it in the Aeon setting - I doubt even the Doyen have explored ALL of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-07-2018, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T18:51:14-08:00","id":1273367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1185538-kickstarter-preview-discussion-\u00e6on-01-06-spoilers?p=1273348#post1273348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I know I'm super late on this, but this thread still seems like the best place for general questions. If the limit for teleportation jumps is within the same galaxy, how do jump ships cross lightyears of space? Do they do that in multiple jumps or does some part of the ship help them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As others have suggested, you may be confusing galaxies and solar systems. The closest star to Earth is Promixma Centauri, and it's 4.2 light years away. The USS Voyager in <i>Star Trek: Voyager</i> was kicked 70,000 light years away and had an extremely long journey ahead of it to return home. Both Proxima Centauri and the destination of the USS Voyager are within the Milky Way galaxy. If Leviathans are limited to travel within our galaxy that doesn't really pose a problem.<br /> <br /> Nearly the entirety of Star Trek and the Mass Effect trilogy takes place within the Milky Way. it's plenty big.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby"